= \\\"circuit\\\") resolveCircuitWalls(race);\",\"old_line\":973,\"new_string\":\"if (race.course.kind === \\\"circuit\\\") resolveCircuitWalls(race, dt);\",\"new_line\":973,\"context_before\":\"    const input = kart.cpu ? cpuInput(race, kart) : provided || neutralAction();\\n    stepKart(race, kart, input, dt);\\n  });\\n\",\"context_after\":\"  else resolveArena(race);\\n  resolveKarts(race);\\n  resolveCone(race);\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"  \"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"baf7d9ac-6b2f-41b8-87a2-cefb92a8c3f6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_27","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The kart's wallLock property must be initialized to prevent undefined errors.\n\nThe wallLock logic is confirmed. I am now writing scene.js, main.js, audio, style, and credits. The credits will include a placeholder for issues caught during testing.\n\nUI rendering will stay in main.js rather than a separate file. The module will contain functions for mounting, screen rendering, HUD updates, map drawing, input polling, menu handling, match startup, and the main frame loop.\n\nThe map renderer is being implemented with canvas projection. Course bounds are scaled to fit the canvas with padding, and a centering offset is calculated. X and Z coordinates are mapped to screen space using a shared scale factor. The track outline will be drawn in a light brown stroke.\n\nThe map renderer now draws circuit tracks as closed paths and rectangular layouts as boxes. Karts are drawn as colored circles, with the local player highlighted in gold.\n\nArrow and space key presses will be intercepted to prevent page scrolling. Pointer lock will activate on canvas click during races. Settings will persist in localStorage and load automatically at startup.\n\nThe settings persistence logic now also saves the best trial time. Menu edge detection will use a four-frame history buffer to prevent repeated inputs.\n\nThe menu edge detection now covers confirm, back, and pause buttons alongside directional inputs. A new helper function detects any active input from keyboards, mouse, or gamepads to trigger the attract mode.\n\nGamepad input detection now includes analog stick thresholds. When exiting attract mode, the current frame will be swallowed to prevent accidental title menu activation. The mouse state object tracks movement deltas, button presses, and wheel events, with pointer-locked canvas movement captured via movementX.\n\nMouse movement deltas will be reset at the end of each frame. Menu confirm actions will be handled exclusively by click handlers to avoid double-firing with keyboard input. During races, mouse buttons will drive kart movement only while pointer lock is active on the canvas.\n\nMouse wheel input will trigger item use. The results screen now handles cup continue, retry, and finished states differently. Cup continue advances to the next course with the same character. Cup retry restarts the current course. Cup finished displays standings before returning to the title screen. Versus, battle, and trial modes all return to the title on confirm. Trial mode records the best time when a kart finishes.\n\nThe results screen will display the player's best time and points. Cup results are recorded once per race using a `recorded` flag to prevent duplicates. Retrying a cup does not increment the counter, while continuing advances to the next course. The finished state returns to the title and clears the cup data. Attract mode bypasses the results screen entirely. Pausing and quiting exits to the title, clears the active race, and restores the menu diorama. A `destroySim` helper is being added to properly dispose of the simulation view.\n\nThe mountSim function now destroys the old simulation before creating a new physics world and scene view. A parked race for the menu diorama is defined with eight entrants: four human characters and four CPUs.\n\nThe parked race simulation will not step physics so the menu diorama remains static with countdown timers and item boxes visible. Real races replace this simulation, and returning to the menu remounts it. The boot sequence starts with the cinder course in parked mode, while attract mode mounts its own race and steps it. DOM elements for goShow and countdown will be added. Scene.js and main.js are ready to be written.\n\nThe disposeView function will use a Set to track shared geometries and prevent double-disposal. Unique materials will be collected in a Set to avoid nulling cached toon programs during cleanup.\n\nuserData will be attached to kart objects so the animation loop can locate their wheels. The arena floor plane is rotated -90 degrees on the X axis so it lies flat on the XZ ground plane.\n\nArena walls will be four box meshes. Obstacles include pillars and crates built from CylinderGeometry and BoxGeometry. Static balloons will decorate the scene. Kart characters will have two eye boxes for faces, with hair styles chosen by character ID.\n\nThe hair function clones geometry for Pip's ears to save memory. A nose wedge is being added as a scaled box on the kart chassis front.\n\nThe kart nose is positioned at the front of the chassis. Orange flame spheres will sit behind the kart and ignore shadows. Spark particles will use a bright yellow basic material. The held item mesh will change color dynamically during animation based on its kind.\n\nMeshBasicNodeMaterial will be used for small effects so color updates remain reliable. The HTML build must avoid `</script>` and `-->` sequences in the about text. I will draft honest credits with placeholder issue counts, then run a final grep to strip any TODOs or stubs before shipping.\n\nTwo product bugs were found and fixed: the respawn clock ignored stalls longer than three seconds, and wall impacts retriggered every step. The invert-zero issue was a test expectation bug, not a product defect. The item-class state test was the most helpful, while the touch-gate boolean test was least helpful. Engine and prompt feedback sections will be drafted as planned. The build date will be set to a static string updated at the end of the process.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-abc648a4-185d-4650-931d-5ba1a04866a6-47","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/race.js","old_string":"slowT: 0,","new_string":"slowT: 0,\n    wallLock: 0,"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-abc648a4-185d-4650-931d-5ba1a04866a6-48","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/audio.js","content":"export function createAudio() {\n  const Ctx = typeof window !== \"undefined\" ? window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext : null;\n  let ctx = null;\n  let noise = null;\n  const engines = [];\n\n  function ac() {\n    if (!Ctx) return null;\n    if (!ctx) ctx = new Ctx();\n    if (ctx.state === \"suspended\") ctx.resume();\n    return ctx;\n  }\n\n  function tone(freq, dur, type, gainValue, slide) {\n    const audio = ac();\n    if (!audio) return;\n    const osc = audio.createOscillator();\n    const gain = audio.createGain();\n    osc.type = type;\n    osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(freq, audio.currentTime);\n    if (slide) osc.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(Math.max(40, freq * slide), audio.currentTime + dur);\n    gain.gain.setValueAtTime(gainValue, audio.currentTime);\n    gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, audio.currentTime + dur);\n    osc.connect(gain);\n    gain.connect(audio.destination);\n    osc.start();\n    osc.stop(audio.currentTime + dur + 0.02);\n  }\n\n  function burst() {\n    const audio = ac();\n    if (!audio) return;\n    if (!noise) {\n      const len = Math.floor(audio.sampleRate * 0.25);\n      noise = audio.createBuffer(1, len, audio.sampleRate);\n      const data = noise.getChannelData(0);\n      for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) data[i] = (Math.random() * 2 - 1) * (1 - i / len);\n    }\n    const src = audio.createBufferSource();\n    src.buffer = noise;\n    const gain = audio.createGain();\n    const filter = audio.createBiquadFilter();\n    filter.type = \"lowpass\";\n    filter.frequency.value = 420;\n    gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.35, audio.currentTime);\n    gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, audio.currentTime + 0.22);\n    src.connect(filter);\n    filter.connect(gain);\n    gain.connect(audio.destination);\n    src.start();\n  }\n\n  return {\n    unlock() {\n      ac();\n    },\n    countdown(value) {\n      if (value === 0) tone(880, 0.28, \"square\", 0.08, 1);\n      else tone(520, 0.12, \"square\", 0.06, 1);\n    },\n    item() {\n      tone(660, 0.08, \"square\", 0.05, 1.8);\n      tone(990, 0.1, \"square\", 0.04, 1);\n    },\n    impact() {\n      burst();\n    },\n    engine(index, speed) {\n      const audio = ac();\n      if (!audio) return;\n      if (!engines[index]) {\n        const osc = audio.createOscillator();\n        const gain = audio.createGain();\n        osc.type = \"sawtooth\";\n        osc.frequency.value = 70;\n        gain.gain.value = 0.0001;\n        osc.connect(gain);\n        gain.connect(audio.destination);\n        osc.start();\n        engines[index] = { osc, gain };\n      }\n      const engine = engines[index];\n      const moving = Math.abs(speed);\n      engine.osc.frequency.setTargetAtTime(58 + moving * 4.2, audio.currentTime, 0.08);\n      engine.gain.gain.setTargetAtTime(moving > 0.4 ? 0.03 : 0.012, audio.currentTime, 0.1);\n    },\n    silence() {\n      if (!ctx) return;\n      for (const engine of engines) {\n        if (engine) engine.gain.gain.setTargetAtTime(0.0001, ctx.currentTime, 0.05);\n      }\n    },\n  };\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":838,"output_tokens":4407,"cache_read_input_tokens":172288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"87d56f77-fef3-402d-9ca5-c7a35b18d606"}
