markup contains those same blocks, and a search of the shipped page and bundled sources shows no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, or stubbed feature. Also confirm `three@0.180` (or an equivalent r180 pin), a WebGPU renderer, no `WebGLRenderer` fallback path, Rapier 0.19.3, Web Audio, `getGamepads` / Gamepad API, a cel/toon material or ramp, an animation update in the render loop, the exact string \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\", invert-axis settings, and a 10-second attract idle threshold.\"},{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\"3. gating: Serve the real root HTML over localhost HTTP (WebGPU needs a secure context; `file://` must not be the launch path). If a headless browser is available (Playwright is expected), load the page twice and capture console plus DOM text to `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.log` and `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.log`. Both runs must agree. Pass only if the visible product title is the chosen riff (not \\\"Mario Kart\\\", \\\"TODO\\\", or an empty title) and a menu control to start play is present, with no unexpected page error; the canvas drawing buffer matches its layout size when WebGPU initializes. If WebGPU or a secure context is unavailable, the page must show that WebGPU and a local server are required rather than a blank screen or a WebGL view. Do not take screenshots and do not grade pixels (TASK.md forbids screenshots and visual review). If the browser cannot start for environmental reasons, save that failure output to `{SCRATCH}/launch-env.log`; criteria 1–2 static checks plus the unit tests are then the a [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":24,\"content\":\"- Inlining CDN libraries into the HTML when a pinned external URL is enough.\"},{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"- Work root is this folder (currently only `TASK.md`). New dev subfolder plus one root HTML file as named in criterion 1.\"},{\"line_number\":30,\"content\":\"- Pure race, item, mode, attract, and input-mapping logic lives in modules the page bundle and the node tests both load. Course geometry, materials, audio buffers, and the HTML shell may stay in the dev folder until bundled.\"},{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\"Keep rules (input mapping including invert, kart handling, laps and rank, item roulette and effects, cup/versus/time-trial/battle transitions, attract timer) in pure functions with no DOM, WebGPU, or audio inside them so node tests call the real code. A thin shell owns the Rapier world, Three.js r180 WebGPU scene, cel materials, animation update, Web Audio triggers, gamepad polling, and split-view cameras, and calls those functions each frame. Bundle the shell and modules into the single root HTML; load Three and Rapier from pinned CDNs if easier. On `file://` or a missing WebGPU adapter, show the server/WebGPU requirement and stop. Pick the title by executing an RNG over the 50 riffs and write the list plus the pick into the HTML comment. Fill About/Credits from the same text.\"},{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"## Task checklist\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"- [ ] Run an RNG over 50 original riff titles, record the pick, and create the dev subfolder plus the named root HTML shell.\"},{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"- [ ] Bundle to the single root HTML with r180 WebGPU and Rapier 0.19.3, no WebGL fallback, and a clear file:// / no-WebGPU message. Remove every TODO, placeholder, and stub.\"},{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"- [ ] Run the unit suite twice and the localhost launch twice; write the logs under `{SCRATCH}`. Put Source Information, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback in the HTML comment, the About screen, and the final reply.\"},{\"line_number\":48,\"content\":\"- The final chat reply is not in the repo. Verifiers confirm Source Information, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback in the HTML comment and About/Credits screen; the reply requirement is the implementer's and cannot be proven from files alone.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d5