{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_36","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Kart movement is analyzed in the frame. Heading 0 maps to velocity (0, 0, +1), which corresponds to positive z.\n\nThe kart's visual front (nose and eyes) sits at local +z. The flame sits at local -z. With rotation.y set to heading, positive values rotate the kart CCW from above. Heading 0 keeps the nose pointing forward. Heading π/2 rotates the nose toward +x.\n\nThe camera sits behind the kart and looks at the nose. A small standalone test will verify that the local +z nose offset aligns with velocity after rotation, confirming the frame convention without Three.js.\n\nThe rotation matrix confirms that a point at local +z becomes (sin θ, 0, cos θ) under Three.js Y-axis rotation. This matches the kart velocity exactly.\n\nA short comment will be added to scene.js near the rotation.y assignment to document the yaw convention. The pause bug fix and keyboard pause from the pause screen are next.\n\nThe pause edge detection will be computed before the menuAction assignment, and keyboard input will be allowed in addition to pads[0]. Camera clones per port will be used in renderViews for safety. The render catch block needs review to prevent repeated console errors.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-49b66726-54e5-4966-b2c6-20c1ccef6856-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/TASK.md","offset":40,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-49b66726-54e5-4966-b2c6-20c1ccef6856-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/main.js","offset":740,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-49b66726-54e5-4966-b2c6-20c1ccef6856-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/m