{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_63","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Playwright is a Python package.\n\nA Python Playwright script will launch Chromium headless to load the page. It will wait for the dataset boot gate with a 25-second timeout. Console errors, page text, and canvas size will be collected. WebGPU may need unsafe flags in headless mode. If unavailable, the gate message is the correct outcome.\n\nWebGPU flags will be passed to Chromium to enable the game. The server will run on port 8767. WSL may crash or hit memory limits, so only one browser instance is used at a time. Viewport-matrix and channel arguments are unnecessary.\n\nThe server will run from the work root in the background. CDN modules like Three.js and Rapier are required for boot, so network access is essential. If the network is blocked, the boot gate remains pending and the title stays static. A visible title and start button without running JavaScript would indicate a network or environment issue.\n\nA blank successful load is a product failure. The verifier might accept static HTML, but JavaScript must actually execute. Console output and boot state will be logged to detect pending boot. A pageerror listener will catch module loading failures.\n\nThe script will launch the browser twice in separate contexts to match the plan. Both runs will record logs. The boot timeout is raised to 30 seconds to allow for module loading and scene building.\n\nThe script will use `wait_for_function` to poll the boot dataset attribute until it reaches \"ready\" or \"gate\", with a 30-second timeout. If that wait throws, the script will still capture the current page state and console output. The Playwright synchronous API is being drafted with Chromium launched headless at 1280 by 720 pixels.\n\nThe script will evaluate JavaScript in the browser to read the canvas element, product title, start button, and gate state directly from the DOM.\n\nThe script will also capture the first 2000 characters of body text, canvas dimensions, and touch gate content. Navigator.gpu will be recorded in the evaluation. When boot reaches ready, the script will verify that canvas width matches clientWidth because fitBuffer uses clientWidth.\n\nThe canvas width should match clientWidth after initialization. devicePixelRatio is forced to 1. The body has overflow hidden to prevent scrollbars from reducing clientWidth. The server must start before Playwright runs. earlyoom could kill the browser process.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7dad0a74-3cd5-42ef-bcfa-4b6e156b3d31-78","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/launch.py","content":"import json\nimport sys\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nurl = sys.argv[1]\nout = sys.argv[2]\nlines = []\n\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True, args=[\n        \"--enable-unsafe-webgpu\",\n        \"--enable-features=WebGPU\",\n    ])\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={\"width\": 1280, \"height\": 720})\n    page.on(\"console\", lambda msg: lines.append(f\"console.{msg.type}: {msg.text}\"))\n    page.on(\"pageerror\", lambda err: lines.append(f\"pageerror: {err}\"))\n    page.goto(url, wait_until=\"domcontentloaded\", timeout=45000)\n    try:\n        page.wait_for_function(\n            \"() => document.body.dataset.boot === 'ready' || document.body.dataset.boot === 'gate'\",\n            timeout=30000,\n        )\n    except Exception as exc:\n        lines.append(f\"wait-failed: {exc}\")\n    page.wait_for_timeout(400)\n    info = page.evaluate(\n        \"\"\"() => {\n          const canvas = document.getElementById('view');\n          const title = document.getElementById('product-title');\n          const start = document.getElementById('start-game');\n          const gate = document.getElementById('gate');\n          const touch = document.getElementById('touch-gate');\n          return {\n            boot: document.body.dataset.boot || '',\n            title: title ? title.textContent : '',\n            start: start ? start.textContent : '',\n            startId: start ? start.id : '',\n            gateHidden: gate ? gate.hidden : null,\n            gateText: gate ? gate.textContent : '',\n            touchText: touch ? touch.innerText : '',\n            href: location.href,\n            protocol: location.protocol,\n            secure: window.isSecureContext,\n            hasGpu: !!navigator.gpu,\n            canvasWidth: canvas ? canvas.width : 0,\n            canvasHeight: canvas ? canvas.height : 0,\n            clientWidth: canvas ? canvas.clientWidth : 0,\n            clientHeight: canvas ? canvas.clientHeight : 0,\n            bodyText: (document.body.innerText || '').slice(0, 2500),\n          };\n        }\"\"\"\n    )\n    browser.close()\n\nreport = {\"info\": info, \"log\": lines}\ntext = json.dumps(report, indent=2)\nwith open(out, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:\n    handle.write(text)\nprint(text)\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7dad0a74-3cd5-42ef-bcfa-4b6e156b3d31-79","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 -m http.server 8767 --bind 127.0.0.1","description":"Serve the work root over localhost HTTP","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":550,"output_tokens":2144,"cache_read_input_tokens":119680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"5883dc47-58cd-4a89-93ef-a054fa5860bf"}
