{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d85f3021-2e9c-4f7a-96b1-d4a884bd3192-91","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"55410→\\t\\tthis.setViewport( 0, 0, width, height );\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( this._initialized ) this.backend.updateSize();\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n\\t * Sets the size of the renderer.\\n\\t *\\n\\t * @param {number} width - The width in logical pixels.\\n55420→\\t * @param {number} height - The height in logical pixels.\\n\\t * @param {boolean} [updateStyle=true] - Whether to update the `style` attribute of the canvas or not.\\n\\t */\\n\\tsetSize( width, height, updateStyle = true ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t// Renderer can't be resized while presenting in XR.\\n\\t\\tif ( this.xr && this.xr.isPresenting ) return;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis._width = width;\\n\\t\\tthis._height = height;\\n55430→\\n\\t\\tthis.domElement.width = Math.floor( width * this._pixelRatio );\\n\\t\\tthis.domElement.height = Math.floor( height * this._pixelRatio );\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( updateStyle === true ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tthis.domElement.style.width = width + 'px';\\n\\t\\t\\tthis.domElement.style.height = height + 'px';\\n\\n\\t\\t}\\n55440→\\n\\t\\tthis.setViewport( 0, 0, width, height );\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( this._initialized ) this.backend.updateSize();\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n\\t * Defines a manual sort function for the opaque render list.\\n\\t * Pass `null` to use the default sort.\",\"content_concise\":\"55410→\\t\\tthis.setViewport( 0, 0, width, height );\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( this._initialized ) this.backend.updateSize();\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n\\t * Sets the size of the renderer.\\n\\t *\\n\\t * @param {number} width - The width in logical pixels.\\n55420→\\t * @param {number} height - The height in logical pixels.\\n\\t * @param {boolean} [updateStyle=true] - Whether to update the `style` attribute of the canvas or not.\\n\\t */\\n\\tsetSize( width, height, updateStyle = true ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t// Renderer can't be resized while presenting in XR.\\n\\t\\tif ( this.xr && this.xr.isPresenting ) return;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis._width = width;\\n\\t\\tthis._height = height;\\n55430→\\n\\t\\tthis.domElement.width = Math.floor( width * this._pixelRatio );\\n\\t\\tthis.domElement.height = Math.floor( height * this._pixelRatio );\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( updateStyle === true ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tthis.domElement.style.width = width + 'px';\\n\\t\\t\\tthis.domElement.style.height = height + 'px';\\n\\n\\t\\t}\\n55440→\\n\\t\\tthis.setViewport( 0, 0, width, height );\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( this._initialized ) this.backend.updateSize();\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n\\t * Defines a manual sort function for the opaque render list.\\n\\t * Pass `null` to use the default sort.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/three.webgpu.js\",\"offset\":55410,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"\\t\\tthis.setViewport( 0, 0, width, height );\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( this._initialized ) this.backend.updateSize();\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n\\t * Sets the size of the renderer.\\n\\t *\\n\\t * @param {number} width - The width in logical pixels.\\n\\t * @param {number} height - The height in logical pixels.\\n\\t * @param {boolean} [updateStyle=true] - Whether to update the `style` attribute of the canvas or not.\\n\\t */\\n\\tsetSize( width, height, updateStyle = true ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t// Renderer can't be resized while presenting in XR.\\n\\t\\tif ( this.xr && this.xr.isPresenting ) return;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis._width = width;\\n\\t\\tthis._height = height;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.domElement.width = Math.floor( width * this._pixelRatio );\\n\\t\\tthis.domElement.height = Math.floor( height * this._pixelRatio );\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( updateStyle === true ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tthis.domElement.style.width = width + 'px';\\n\\t\\t\\tthis.domElement.style.height = height + 'px';\\n\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.setViewport( 0, 0, width, height );\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( this._initialized ) this.backend.updateSize();\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n\\t * Defines a manual sort function for the opaque render list.\\n\\t * Pass `null` to use the default sort.\\n\",\"total_lines\":77115}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"af315014-9c79-4544-b8c1-1225d34ba6d7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_74","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `setSize` function sets `domElement.width` on every call, even when the value hasn't changed.\n\nRepeatedly setting `canvas.width` to the same value may reset the WebGPU context. This would destroy the GPU device and cause `device.lost` every frame after initialization, leading to silent render failures.\n\nThe fix is to only call `setSize` when the width or height actually changes. Three.js currently assigns `canvas.width` unconditionally, so the check must happen before the renderer update.\n\nThe fix adds a guard to `fitBuffer` that only calls `renderer.setSize` when the canvas dimensions or pixel ratio differ from the current values. This prevents redundant updates and preserves the WebGPU context during initialization.\n\nSetting canvas.width before getContext is standard practice and safe. The first fitBuffer call should see matching dimensions because the canvas is already in the DOM with CSS width 100%.\n\nSkipping `setSize` when dimensions match could leave the renderer's internal size at its default. The canvas buffer would already be correct, but the renderer might render at the wrong internal resolution.\n\nThe launch log confirms the canvas width was 1280 after the race, but it was only maintained because `setSize` ran every frame. Repeatedly resetting `canvas.width` likely destroyed the WebGPU device. The fix is to call `setSize` once immediately after initialization so the renderer registers the correct size, then only update when the actual dimensions change.\n\nSetting `canvas.width` to the same value still clears the bitmap per the HTML spec. It is unclear whether this also destroys the WebGPU device.\n\nI will test whether a single `setSize` call after initialization still destroys the device. If it does, the problem likely lies elsewhere. I will also verify this with a minimal Three.js page.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b45243a1-5b29-421f-8caf-7b0e83d73d91-92","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/scene.js","old_string":"export function fitBuffer(canvas, renderer) {\n  const width = Math.max(1, Math.floor(canvas.clientWidth || window.innerWidth || 1));\n  const height = Math.max(1, Math.floor(canvas.clientHeight || window.innerHeight || 1));\n  if (renderer) {\n    renderer.setPixelRatio(1);\n    renderer.setSize(width, height, false);\n  } else {\n    canvas.width = width;\n    canvas.height = height;\n  }\n  return { width, height };\n}","new_string":"const fitted = { width: 0, height: 0 };\n\nexport function fitBuffer(canvas, renderer) {\n  const width = Math.max(1, Math.floor(canvas.clientWidth || window.innerWidth || 1));\n  const height = Math.max(1, Math.floor(canvas.clientHeight || window.innerHeight || 1));\n  if (renderer) {\n    if (fitted.width !== width || fitted.height !== height) {\n      renderer.setPixelRatio(1);\n      renderer.setSize(width, height, false);\n      fitted.width = width;\n      fitted.height = height;\n    }\n  } else if (canvas.width !== width || canvas.height !== height) {\n    canvas.width = width;\n    canvas.height = height;\n  }\n  return { width, height };\n}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":462,"output_tokens":1659,"cache_read_input_tokens":131072,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"721a81d4-f3d3-4046-a143-2a8b63e4fda3"}
