{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_90","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"WSL GPU paravirtualization is available via /dev/dxg. nvidia-smi is present.\n\nChromium 153 headless may be using a broken software WebGPU instead of the NVIDIA GPU. I am testing Chromium flags to force the Dawn D3D12 backend through WSL's dxg interface.\n\n`--ignore-gpu-blocklist` and `--enable-gpu` are being tested. Playwright's `headless=True` may be triggering GPU issues in Chromium 153. A headed browser might bypass the failure if WSLg is available.\n\nThe browser started successfully, so device loss is not an environmental startup failure. The page should display the gate message instead of a blank canvas and console error. I will try one quick flag set to force a real render. If that fails, I will override onDeviceLost to show the gate cleanly without console errors. The final launch logs should show either a working race or a clean gate.\n\nA targeted flag set is being tested to force a real GPU render. A quick probe will wait for boot and print console output and adapter info instead of playing the full game.\n\nThe probe will use the full toon renderer and complete scene instead of the tiny mode. setSize is being restored for proper buffer matching. Shadows are being re-enabled unless the GPU device dies.\n\nAntialias is being set to false for safety. Shadows are being left off because PCF on WebGPU is a known footgun and the cel ramp does not need them. The tiny scene branch and debug marks will be removed before the final build but kept for this probe.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-11968882-429d-48e5-a8ad-007ebd6d8155-111","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/scene.js","old_string":"    const material = new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color, side });","new_string":"    const material = new THREE.MeshToonNodeMaterial({ color, gradientMap: gradient, side });"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-11968882-429d-48e5-a8ad-007ebd6d8155-112","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/scene.js","old_string":"  if (renderer) {\n    fitted.width = width;\n    fitted.height = height;\n  } else if (canvas.width !== width || canvas.height !== height) {","new_string":"  if (renderer) {\n    if (fitted.width !== width || fitted.height !== height) {\n      renderer.setPixelRatio(1);\n      renderer.setSize(width, height, false);\n      fitted.width = width;\n      fitted.height = height;\n    }\n  } else if (canvas.width !== width || canvas.height !== height) {"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-11968882-429d-48e5-a8ad-007ebd6d8155-113","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/scene.js","old_string":"export function buildScene(course, race) {\n  if (globalThis.__KART_TINY) {\n    const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n    scene.background = new THREE.Color(0x335588);\n    const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(2, 2, 2), new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color: 0xff8800 }));\n    scene.add(mesh);\n    scene.add(new THREE.AmbientLight(0xffffff, 1));\n    const cameras = [0, 1, 2, 3].map(() => new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(68, 1, 0.1, 100));\n    cameras.forEach((camera) => camera.position.set(0, 2, 6));\n    return { scene, camera: cameras[0], cameras, karts: [], boxes: [], dynamics: new THREE.Group(), cone: mesh, gradient: null, course };\n  }\n  const gradient = gradientTexture();","new_string":"export function buildScene(course, race) {\n  const gradient = gradientTexture();"}},{"type":"tool_use