5,122,97,116,105,111,110,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,59,32,112,97,115,115,32,97,32,115,105,110,103,108,101,32,111,98,106,101,99,116,32,105,110,115,116,101,97,100,34,44,10,32,32,32,32,34,99,111,110,115,111,108,101,46,108,111,103,58,32,77,65,82,75,32,108,111,116,34,44,10,32,32,32,32,34,99,111,110,115,111,108,101,46,108,111,103,58,32,77,65,82,75,32,114,101,110,100,101,114,34,44,10,32,32,32,32,34,99,111,110,115,111,108,101,46,108,111,103,58,32,77,65,82,75,32,97,102,116,101,114,45,98,111,111,116,34,44,10,32,32,32,32,34,99,111,110,115,111,108,101,46,108,111,103,58,32,77,65,82,75,32,97,102,116,101,114,45,114,97,99,101,34,44,10,32,32,32,32,34,99,111,110,115,111,108,101,46,108,111,103,58,32,77,65,82,75,32,97,102,116,101,114,45,119,97,105,116,34,10,32,32,93,10,125,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\nwrote /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html (129435 bytes)\\n(node:140510) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n{\\n  \\\"info\\\": {\\n    \\\"boot\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Kartesian Derby\\\",\\n    \\\"start\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"startId\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"gateHidden\\\": true,\\n    \\\"gateText\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"touchText\\\": \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\\n  Settings\\\",\\n    \\\"href\\\": \\\"http://127.0.0.1:8767/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html\\\",\\n    \\\"protocol\\\": \\\"http:\\\",\\n    \\\"secure\\\": true,\\n    \\\"hasGpu\\\": true,\\n    \\\"canvasWidth\\\": 1280,\\n    \\\"canvasHeight\\\": 720,\\n    \\\"clientWidth\\\": 1280,\\n    \\\"clientHeight\\\": 720,\\n    \\\"bodyText\\\": \\\"1st\\\\nLap 1 / 3\\\\n0 km/h\\\\nEmpty\\\\n1 Pip\\\\n2 Pip 1\\\\n3 Quill\\\\n4 Bramble\\\\n5 Holt\\\\n6 Pip 5\\\\n7 Quill 6\\\\n8 Bramble 7\\\\n\\\\n3\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"log\\\": [\\n    \\\"console.log: MARK renderer\\\",\\n    \\\"console.log: MARK sized\\\",\\n    \\\"console.warning: using deprecated parameters for the initialization function; pass a single object instead\\\",\\n    \\\"console.log: MARK lot\\\",\\n    \\\"console.log: MARK render\\\",\\n    \\\"console.log: MARK after-boot\\\",\\n    \\\"console.log: MARK after-race\\\",\\n    \\\"console.log: MARK after-wait\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637 && node build.mjs && export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 && python3 /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/launch.py \\\"http://127.0.0.1:8767/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html\\\" /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/launch-diag.log\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Retry WebGPU render with Vulkan ANGLE flags\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on%2Fwork/01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862/terminal/call-6761d4f2-98a2-429e-8f33-59a3babd075f-116.log\",\"total_bytes\":1328}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"2945796a-15dc-4157-a60b-8ede7a64dafa"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_92","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Vulkan flags fixed the device loss.\n\nThe race runs cleanly at 1280x720 with no console errors. Next I will strip the MARK debug logs from main.js and launch.py, rebuild the final HTML without them, and run the launch script twice to official logs.\n\nThe Rapier warning is a library message, not an unexpected page error. I will test passing an empty object to `RAPIER.init({})` to silence it.\n\nThe deprecated `init(module, options)` signature is the source of the warning. Passing an empty object to `init({})` should silence it and fix unit test output too. I will write stack-notes.md, update the plan checklist, and grep for banned words.\n\nThe every-frame canvas resize was a real bug that destroyed the drawing buffer. I stopped resizing the canvas each frame to prevent context resets. The device loss was caused by missing Vulkan flags in the launch harness, not a game logic error.\n\nThe every-frame resize is now guarded so it only runs when the size actually changes. The diagnostic tests confirmed that the headless Chromium GPU backend itself was the root cause of the device loss, not the scene or the resize logic.\n\nThe testing feedback will note that the device loss was caused by default headless Chromium flags, not a game logic bug. The retry with Vulkan ANGLE succeeded and produced valid lap, place, and speed data. The critical count remains one for the road winding.\n\nI will add an `onDeviceLost` override to the renderer so a lost GPU shows the required gate sentence instead of a blank canvas. This makes the page more resilient without affecting the successful launch path.\n\nThe `onDeviceLost` handler is now wired to show the required gate sentence. I will strip the debug marks from main.js and launch.py, update the credits testing section with the launch finding, and rebuild before running the final two launches.\n\nThe testing feedback draft is finalized. It notes the headless device loss was caused by missing Vulkan flags, not a game bug. The resize guard is confirmed to prevent frame-by-frame canvas resets. Shadows are disabled because the plan specifies cel/toon quantized lighting, so no deviation is needed.\n\nI will record in stack notes that shadows were disabled as an extra GPU optimization for the toon ramp. Antialiasing remains off. Unit tests need no rerun because they do not import scene.js. I will grep sources for TODOs and WebGLRenderer references, kill the server after the final launches, and strip the remaining MARK markers from main.js before building.\n\nI will strip the extra console.log marks from launch.py so the saved logs do not contain MARK strings, while keeping the about and race flow intact so the log proves the race HUD.\n\nBoth launch logs must match after the final build. I also noticed the start button is empty during the race because the title panel clears and hides it, but the initial HTML and title screen still satisfy the plan's menu control requirement.\n\nI will update the launch script to save both a title snapshot and a race snapshot. The title snapshot will show the start button, and the race snapshot will show the HUD. This gives strict proof that the menu control was present before the race began.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-781a687a-ce65-4857-b760-4c004ff9b6f2-117","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on%2Fwork/01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862/goal/plan.md","offset":36,"limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-781a687a-ce65-4857-b760-4c004ff9b6f2-118","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/main.js","old_string":"    renderer = await createRenderer(canvas);\n    console.log(\"MARK renderer\");\n    fitBuffer(canvas, renderer);\n    console.log(\"MARK sized\");\n    await showLot();\n    console.log(\"MARK lot\");\n    document.body.dataset.boot = \"ready\";\n    requestAnimationFrame(frame);","new_string":"    renderer = await createRenderer(canvas);\n    renderer.onDeviceLost = () => {\n      showGate(\"WebGPU and a local server are required.\");\n    };\n    fitBuffer(canvas, renderer);\n    await showLot();\n    document.body.dataset.boot = \"ready\";\n    requestAnimationFrame(frame);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-781a687a-ce65-4857-b760-4c004ff9b6f2-119","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/main.js","old_string":"let markedRender = false;\n\nfunction renderViews(dt, time) {\n  if (!renderer || !sim) return;\n  if (!markedRender) {\n    markedRender = true;\n    console.log(\"MARK render\");\n  }","new_string":"function renderViews(dt, time) {\n  if (!renderer || !sim) return;"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-781a687a-ce65-4857-b760-4c004ff9b6f2-120","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js","old_string":"How many issues did testing catch? The first suite run failed 2 tests. One was a product timer: a single step longer than 3 seconds never finished a 5 second item-box return, because the race clamped each call to 3 seconds. The cap is now 8 seconds. The other failure was the test itself: the stick sample never crossed the menu threshold, so it compared 0 with -0. A frame check of the road strip found the triangles wound downward, which would hide the track from above. That winding is reversed and the suite now asserts an upward normal. The pause Start edge was stored before it was read, so it could not resume; the Resume row still could. Wall hits also fired on every step while a kart stayed against a wall; they now wait 0.4 seconds.","new_string":"How many issues did testing catch? The first suite run failed 2 tests. One was a product timer: a single step longer than 3 seconds never finished a 5 second item-box return, because the race clamped each call to 3 seconds. The cap is now 8 seconds. The other failure was the test itself: the stick sample never crossed the menu threshold, so it compared 0 with -0. A frame check of the road strip found the triangles wound downward, which would hide the track from above. That winding is reversed and the suite now asserts an upward normal. The pause Start edge was stored before it was read, so it could not resume; the Resume row still could. Wall hits also fired on every step while a kart stayed against a wall; they now wait 0.4 seconds. The headless load lost the WebGPU device under the default GPU flags. Launching Chromium with Vulkan kept the device. The canvas then matched the window, and a cup race showed lap, place, and speed. The buffer is resized only when the window size changes."}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":777,"output_tokens":2574,"cache_read_input_tokens":147072,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"e46facd9-9569-4dde-af62-7e346e5f80c5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-781a687a-ce65-4857-b760-4c004ff9b6f2-117","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"36→## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Run an RNG over 50 original riff titles, record the pick, and create the dev subfolder plus the named root HTML shell.\\n- [ ] Implement pure input, race, item, mode, and attract logic, then the node tests in verification step 2.\\n- [ ] Add two courses, one battle arena, original characters, Rapier 0.19.3 kart collision, cel-shaded WebGPU scene, animation update, HUD, and Web Audio cues.\\n40→- [ ] Wire the 10-foot menu, invert-axis settings, 2/3/4-player splits, cup, versus, time trial, balloon battle, pause, attract mode, touch-only message, and About/Credits.\\n- [ ] Bundle to the single root HTML with r180 WebGPU and Rapier 0.19.3, no WebGL fallback, and a clear file:// / no-WebGPU message. Remove every TODO, placeholder, and stub.\\n- [ ] Run the unit suite twice and the localhost launch twice; write the logs under `{SCRATCH}`. Put Source Information, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback in the HTML comment, the About screen, and the final reply.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md requires WebGPU with no fallback, and WebGPU needs a secure context plus an adapter. Headless Chromium here may lack a working adapter. Do not satisfy that by adding WebGL. Use the launch escape hatch in verification step 3 when the browser cannot start or cannot create an adapter; a blank successful load is still a failure.\\n- TASK.md forbids screenshots and visual review, which conflicts with a pixel-fill launch gate. The launch gate is DOM text, console errors, and canvas buffer size only.\\n- The filename template in TASK.md contains spaces (`GameTitle-SOURCE-...`, SOURCE = \\\"Mario Kart 64 for N64\\\"). This plan hyphenates those spaces so the path is one segment. A file that keeps the spaces but is otherwise identical still meets the template; either form is acceptable if the fixed suffix `grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html` and the source token are present.\\n- The final chat reply is not in the repo. Verifiers confirm Source Information, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback in the HTML comment and About/Credits screen; the reply requirement is the implementer's and cannot be proven from files alone.\\n- Retail MK64 mode count and course count would make the slice unfinishable. Criterion 5 is the defining subset (cup of two courses, versus, time trial, one balloon arena, 8-kart field, full item classes). Anything beyond that is a non-goal, not a silent drop.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"36→## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Run an RNG over 50 original riff titles, record the pick, and create the dev subfolder plus the named root HTML shell.\\n- [ ] Implement pure input, race, item, mode, and attract logic, then the node tests in verification step 2.\\n- [ ] Add two courses, one battle arena, original characters, Rapier 0.19.3 kart collision, cel-shaded WebGPU scene, animation update, HUD, and Web Audio cues.\\n40→- [ ] Wire the 10-foot menu, invert-axis settings, 2/3/4-player splits, cup, versus, time trial, balloon battle, pause, attract mode, touch-only message, and About/Credits.\\n- [ ] Bundle to the single root HTML with r180 WebGPU and Rapier 0.19.3, no WebGL fallback, and a clear file:// / no-WebGPU message. Remove every TODO, placeholder, and stub.\\n- [ ] Run the unit suite twice and the localhost launch twice; write the logs under `{SCRATCH}`. Put Source Information, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback in the HTML comment, the About screen, and the final reply.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md requires WebGPU with no fallback, and WebGPU needs a secure context plus an adapter. Headless Chromium here may lack a working adapter. Do not satisfy that by adding WebGL. Use the launch escape hatch in verification step 3 when the browser cannot start or cannot create an adapter; a blank successful load is still a failure.\\n- TASK.md forbids screenshots and visual review, which conflicts with a pixel-fill launch gate. The launch gate is DOM text, console errors, and canvas buffer size only.\\n- The filename template in TASK.md contains spaces (`GameTitle-SOURCE-...`, SOURCE = \\\"Mario Kart 64 for N64\\\"). This plan hyphenates those spaces so the path is one segment. A file that keeps the spaces but is otherwise identical still meets the template; either form is acceptable if the fixed suffix `grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html` and the source token are present.\\n- The final chat reply is not in the repo. Verifiers confirm Source Information, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback in the HTML comment and About/Credits screen; the reply requirement is the implementer's and cannot be proven from files alone.\\n- Retail MK64 mode count and course count would make the slice unfinishable. Criterion 5 is the defining subset (cup of two courses, versus, time trial, one balloon arena, 8-kart field, full item classes). Anything beyond that is a non-goal, not a silent drop.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on%2Fwork/01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":36,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Run an RNG over 50 original riff titles, record the pick, and create the dev subfolder plus the named root HTML shell.\\n- [ ] Implement pure input, race, item, mode, and attract logic, then the node tests in verification step 2.\\n- [ ] Add two courses, one battle arena, original characters, Rapier 0.19.3 kart collision, cel-shaded WebGPU scene, animation update, HUD, and Web Audio cues.\\n- [ ] Wire the 10-foot menu, invert-axis settings, 2/3/4-player splits, cup, versus, time trial, balloon battle, pause, attract mode, touch-only message, and About/Credits.\\n- [ ] Bundle to the single root HTML with r180 WebGPU and Rapier 0.19.3, no WebGL fallback, and a clear file:// / no-WebGPU message. Remove every TODO, placeholder, and stub.\\n- [ ] Run the unit suite twice and the localhost launch twice; write the logs under `{SCRATCH}`. Put Source Information, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback in the HTML comment, the About screen, and the final reply.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- TASK.md requires WebGPU with no fallback, and WebGPU needs a secure context plus an adapter. Headless Chromium here may lack a working adapter. Do not satisfy that by adding WebGL. Use the launch escape hatch in verification step 3 when the browser cannot start or cannot create an adapter; a blank successful load is still a failure.\\n- TASK.md forbids screenshots and visual review, which conflicts with a pixel-fill launch gate. The launch gate is DOM text, console errors, and canvas buffer size only.\\n- The filename template in TASK.md contains spaces (`GameTitle-SOURCE-...`, SOURCE = \\\"Mario Kart 64 for N64\\\"). This plan hyphenates those spaces so the path is one segment. A file that keeps the spaces but is otherwise identical still meets the template; either form is acceptable if the fixed suffix `grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html` and the source token are present.\\n- The final chat reply is not in the repo. Verifiers confirm Source Information, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback in the HTML comment and About/Credits screen; the reply requirement is the implementer's and cannot be proven from files alone.\\n- Retail MK64 mode count and course count would make the slice unfinishable. Criterion 5 is the defining subset (cup of two courses, versus, time trial, one balloon arena, 8-kart field, full item classes). Anything beyond that is a non-goal, not a silent drop.\\n\",\"total_lines\":49}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-781a687a-ce65-4857-b760-4c004ff9b6f2-118","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"    renderer = await createRenderer(canvas);