ld_string\":\"How many issues did testing catch? The first suite run failed 2 tests. One was a product timer: a single step longer than 3 seconds never finished a 5 second item-box return, because the race clamped each call to 3 seconds. The cap is now 8 seconds. The other failure was the test itself: the stick sample never crossed the menu threshold, so it compared 0 with -0. A frame check of the road strip found the triangles wound downward, which would hide the track from above. That winding is reversed and the suite now asserts an upward normal. The pause Start edge was stored before it was read, so it could not resume; the Resume row still could. Wall hits also fired on every step while a kart stayed against a wall; they now wait 0.4 seconds.\",\"new_string\":\"How many issues did testing catch? The first suite run failed 2 tests. One was a product timer: a single step longer than 3 seconds never finished a 5 second item-box return, because the race clamped each call to 3 seconds. The cap is now 8 seconds. The other failure was the test itself: the stick sample never crossed the menu threshold, so it compared 0 with -0. A frame check of the road strip found the triangles wound downward, which would hide the track from above. That winding is reversed and the suite now asserts an upward normal. The pause Start edge was stored before it was read, so it could not resume; the Resume row still could. Wall hits also fired on every step while a kart stayed against a wall; they now wait 0.4 seconds. The headless load lost the WebGPU device under the default GPU flags. Launching Chromium with Vulkan kept the device. The canvas then matched the window, and a cup race showed lap, place, and speed. The buffer is resized only when the window size changes.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"How many issues did testing catch? The first suite run failed 2 tests. One was a product timer: a single step longer than 3 seconds never finished a 5 second item-box return, because the race clamped each call to 3 seconds. The cap is now 8 seconds. The other failure was the test itself: the stick sample never crossed the menu threshold, so it compared 0 with -0. A frame check of the road strip found the triangles wound downward, which would hide the track from above. That winding is reversed and the suite now asserts an upward normal. The pause Start edge was stored before it was read, so it could not resume; the Resume row still could. Wall hits also fired on every step while a kart stayed against a wall; they now wait 0.4 seconds.\",\"old_line\":13,\"new_string\":\"How many issues did testing catch? The first suite run failed 2 tests. One was a product timer: a single step longer than 3 seconds never finished a 5 second item-box return, because the race clamped each call to 3 seconds. The cap is now 8 seconds. The other failure was the test itself: the stick sample never crossed the menu threshold, so it compared 0 with -0. A frame check of the road strip found the triangles wound downward, which would hide the track from above. That winding is reversed and the suite now asserts an upward normal. The pause Start edge was stored before it was read, so it could not resume; the Resume row still could. Wall hits also fired on every step while a kart stayed against a wall; they now wait 0.4 seconds. The headless load lost the WebGPU device under the default GPU flags. Launching Chromium with Vulkan kept the device. The canvas then matched the window, and a cup race showed lap, place, and speed. The buffer is resized only when the window size changes.\",\"new_line\":13,\"context_before\":\"Usage: unknown\\n\\nTesting Feedback\\n\",\"context_after\":\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 1. The downward road would leave the course invisible. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The pause edge and the wall-hit repeat do not stop a race.\\nWhat was the most helpful test you ran? The item-class test. It starts a fresh race and checks that every shipped item changes speed, control, balloons, or a held item.\\nWhat was the least helpful test you ran? The touch-gate predicate. It only checks three booleans and never opens the page.\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"2e2f5e35-a37c-4762-a1ea-303bb912f909"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_93","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Updating launch.py to capture title state before navigation and removing MARK evaluates.\n\nRebuilding and running twice. Testing init({}) to silence the rapier warning. Verifying onDeviceLost ignores info and shows the gate. Confirmed assigning it after init is safe.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-72d58755-306f-4a3a-bccd-7bfab923b353-121","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/launch.py","old_string":"    page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n    page.evaluate(\"() => console.log('MARK after-boot')\")\n    page.get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"About\").click()","new_string":"    page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n\n    def snap():\n        return page.evaluate(\n            \"\"\"() => {\n              const canvas = document.getElementById('view');\n              const title = document.getElementById('product-title');\n              const start = document.getElementById('start-game');\n              const gate = document.getElementById('gate');\n              const touch = document.getElementById('touch-gate');\n              return {\n                boot: document.body.dataset.boot || '',\n                title: title ? title.textContent : '',\n                start: start ? start.textContent : '',\n                startId: start ? start.id : '',\n                gateHidden: gate ? gate.hidden : null,\n                gateText: gate ? gate.textContent : '',\n                touchText: touch ? touch.innerText.trim() : '',\n                href: location.href,\n                protocol: location.protocol,\n                secure: window.isSecureContext,\n                hasGpu: !!navigator.gpu,\n                canvasWidth: canvas ? canvas.width : 0,\n                canvasHeight: canvas ? canvas.height : 0,\n                clientWidth: canvas ? canvas.clientWidth : 0,\n          