{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_116","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that with `renderContext.clearColor` enabled, the WebGPU render pass uses `GPULoadOp`.\n\n`GPULoadOp.Clear` clears the entire color attachment, not just the scissor rectangle. `setScissorRect` only affects draw calls, not the clear operation. Each `renderer.render()` in the split-screen loop therefore wipes the whole canvas before drawing the current viewport.\n\nOnly the last viewport is visible in the final frame. Earlier renders are fully erased by the clear operation. The other quadrants remain blank or show the background color.\n\nThis is a game-breaking multiplayer bug. It violates Criterion 5, which requires 2-, 3-, and 4-way split views. The viewport and scissor setup is correct, but the default `autoClear` setting is likely true in Three.js. The clear color may also be the scene background.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c06b6567-4339-46ed-938f-d8cdfd6eb66f-47","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"REVISION|autoClear = true|this\\.autoClear","path":"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/three.webgpu.js","head_limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c06b6567-4339-46ed-938f-d8cdfd6eb66f-48","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/three-package.json","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":990,"output_tokens":656,"cache_read_input_tokens":121088,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"2fcca637-1f10-43ce-83c7-9cbe4f980ce4"}
