{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-30df1483-208c-4b49-b7b8-f71669ea45ea-49","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"55220→\\t\\tthis._height = height;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.setViewport( 0, 0, width, height );\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n\\t * The output pass performs tone mapping and color space conversion.\\n\\t *\\n\\t * @private\\n55230→\\t * @param {RenderTarget} renderTarget - The current render target.\\n\\t */\\n\\t_renderOutput( renderTarget ) {\\n\\n\\t\\tconst quad = this._quad;\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( this._nodes.hasOutputChange( renderTarget.texture ) ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tquad.material.fragmentNode = this._nodes.getOutputNode( renderTarget.texture );\\n\\t\\t\\tquad.material.needsUpdate = true;\\n55240→\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t// a clear operation clears the intermediate renderTarget texture, but should not update the screen canvas.\\n\\n\\t\\tconst currentAutoClear = this.autoClear;\\n\\t\\tconst currentXR = this.xr.enabled;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.autoClear = false;\\n\\t\\tthis.xr.enabled = false;\\n55250→\\n\\t\\tthis._renderScene( quad, quad.camera, false );\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.autoClear = currentAutoClear;\\n\\t\\tthis.xr.enabled = currentXR;\\n\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n55260→\\t * Returns the maximum available anisotropy for texture filtering.\\n\\t *\\n\\t * @return {number} The maximum available anisotropy.\\n\\t */\\n\\tgetMaxAnisotropy() {\\n\\n\\t\\treturn this.backend.getMaxAnisotropy();\\n\\n\\t}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"55220→\\t\\tthis._height = height;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.setViewport( 0, 0, width, height );\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n\\t * The output pass performs tone mapping and color space conversion.\\n\\t *\\n\\t * @private\\n55230→\\t * @param {RenderTarget} renderTarget - The current render target.\\n\\t */\\n\\t_renderOutput( renderTarget ) {\\n\\n\\t\\tconst quad = this._quad;\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( this._nodes.hasOutputChange( renderTarget.texture ) ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tquad.material.fragmentNode = this._nodes.getOutputNode( renderTarget.texture );\\n\\t\\t\\tquad.material.needsUpdate = true;\\n55240→\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t// a clear operation clears the intermediate renderTarget texture, but should not update the screen canvas.\\n\\n\\t\\tconst currentAutoClear = this.autoClear;\\n\\t\\tconst currentXR = this.xr.enabled;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.autoClear = false;\\n\\t\\tthis.xr.enabled = false;\\n55250→\\n\\t\\tthis._renderScene( quad, quad.camera, false );\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.autoClear = currentAutoClear;\\n\\t\\tthis.xr.enabled = currentXR;\\n\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n55260→\\t * Returns the maximum available anisotropy for texture filtering.\\n\\t *\\n\\t * @return {number} The maximum available anisotropy.\\n\\t */\\n\\tgetMaxAnisotropy() {\\n\\n\\t\\treturn this.backend.getMaxAnisotropy();\\n\\n\\t}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/three.webgpu.js\",\"offset\":55220,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"\\t\\tthis._height = height;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.setViewport( 0, 0, width, height );\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n\\t * The output pass performs tone mapping and color space conversion.\\n\\t *\\n\\t * @private\\n\\t * @param {RenderTarget} renderTarget - The current render target.\\n\\t */\\n\\t_renderOutput( renderTarget ) {\\n\\n\\t\\tconst quad = this._quad;\\n\\n\\t\\tif ( this._nodes.hasOutputChange( renderTarget.texture ) ) {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tquad.material.fragmentNode = this._nodes.getOutputNode( renderTarget.texture );\\n\\t\\t\\tquad.material.needsUpdate = true;\\n\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\n\\t\\t// a clear operation clears the intermediate renderTarget texture, but should not update the screen canvas.\\n\\n\\t\\tconst currentAutoClear = this.autoClear;\\n\\t\\tconst currentXR = this.xr.enabled;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.autoClear = false;\\n\\t\\tthis.xr.enabled = false;\\n\\n\\t\\tthis._renderScene( quad, quad.camera, false );\\n\\n\\t\\tthis.autoClear = currentAutoClear;\\n\\t\\tthis.xr.enabled = currentXR;\\n\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\t/**\\n\\t * Returns the maximum available anisotropy for texture filtering.\\n\\t *\\n\\t * @return {number} The maximum available anisotropy.\\n\\t */\\n\\tgetMaxAnisotropy() {\\n\\n\\t\\treturn this.backend.getMaxAnisotropy();\\n\\n\\t}\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":77115}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-30df1483-208c-4b49-b7b8-f71669ea45ea-50","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,95,95,101,120,97,109,112,108,101,95,95,118,50,95,95,99,101,108,95,95,102,114,101,101,95,95,101,102,102,105,99,105,101,110,116,95,95,111,110,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"1b34382d-0009-4ae7-a3a6-606d752edea3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_118","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The output pass disables autoClear during canvas blitting.\n\nThe scene renders to an intermediate framebuffer first, then blits the full result to the canvas. Each render therefore replaces the entire canvas with a framebuffer containing only the current viewport.\n\nThe same bug persists: the last viewport overwrites the rest of the canvas with clear color. If the blit copied only the scissored region, split-screen rendering could work. The frame buffer target copies the viewport and scissor state onto the texture. The output pass then draws a full-screen quad of that texture onto the canvas without clearing.\n\nThe full-screen quad blit covers the entire canvas. If the framebuffer is cleared to clear color, the output pass replaces the whole canvas with mostly empty space plus one viewport of content. The only way split-screen could work is if the output quad itself is also scissored to the viewport.\n\nThe output pass calls `_renderScene` with the current viewport and scissor state. If the scissor remains active, the full-screen quad would only draw into that rectangle. Because autoClear is disabled, previous viewports would survive in the rest of the canvas. The key question is whether `_renderOutput` actually respects the scissor.\n\nThe output pass does not switch to the frame buffer target's viewport. Because `useFrameBufferTarget` is false, `_renderScene` keeps the user's original viewport and scissor state. The full-screen quad therefore covers the entire canvas.\n\nThe output quad is scissored to the viewport rectangle. Because autoClear is disabled, only that region updates and previous viewports survive in the rest of the canvas. Split-screen rendering might actually work.\n\nThe first viewport renders to the framebuffer and blits only that scissored region. The second viewport clears the entire framebuffer and draws into its own scissor. The output quad samples that same full framebuffer texture. If it is scissored to the second viewport, it reads only that region from the texture. The first viewport therefore remains intact in the canvas.\n\nThe split-screen path is too uncertain to confirm. Defaulting to refuted would wrongly reject a potentially working implementation.\n\nI will not list the split-screen issue as a definite bug without demonstrating it. The output pass might preserve scissor state, and I have no proof that it does not. Three.js multi-viewport is a known pain point, but r180 may handle this correctly. I will only mention it if I am confident.\n\nHeadless pixel reads are too expensive and forbidden by the plan, so split-screen verification is skipped.\n\nThe pause bug is certain. The outline bug is also certain: the larger shell geometry hides the body because it uses FrontSide, and polygonOffset or culling are not involved.\n\nThis will be reported as a definite bug because the objective requires cel-shaded karts; black shells violate that requirement.\n\nA Node.js simulation of the pause logic is unnecessary because the code is unambiguous; I will cite the relevant lines directly. The settings edge toggling and character cycle duplicate IDs are correct.\n\nThe race HUD capture during the countdown is not a bug. Speed reads zero during the countdown, which is correct. The body text includes lap, position, speed, and held item, satisfying all HUD requirements.\n\nThe pause screen may be invisible because the next frame unpause runs before the browser paints. The pause flag is set, the UI renders, but the unpausing logic executes immediately on the following frame. Since pause is not a racing state, the UI remains visible, yet the pause state clears before the browser can display it.\n\nThe pause menu flashes for about one frame before the next frame unpauses it, so the bug is confirmed. The test file and verification steps do not cover pause behavior, but that omission is not a separate bug.\n\nThe pause bug is in the DOM-coupled shell, not in pure logic modules. The plan requires pure functions to support Node tests, so the shell's pause edge is outside that testable scope. The missing test gap is therefore not a separate finding; the bug itself is the finding. I am now looking for untested bugs in pure logic.\n\nPilfer against an empty target triggers the disruptor spin path. Crownseeker correctly targets second place when the user leads. Brownout skips finished karts. I am now inspecting `lapForProgress` for a possible early lap display bug.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-07521eae-e480-453a-9c29-4395ff03d68d-51","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"1\\.045|BackSide|outline","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-07521eae-e480-453a-9c29-4395ff03d68d-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pauseEdge|menuPrev","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":573,"output_tokens":2439,"cache_read_input_tokens":123776,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"090a3715-86ff-4441-bbbf-551b39211c2a"}
