{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_119","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking the basic() function in the bundle to see if side is set.\n\nConfirmed the source code does not set side. The default MeshBasicNodeMaterial side is FrontSide. No mesh sets side, so shared outline material is not a bug. A keyboard pause bug remains: Escape fires back and resumes because menuPrev.back is stale.\n\nGamepad Options only triggers pause, not back. Keyboard Escape triggers both pause and back. The fix is to seed menuPrev with the current action when transitioning from race to pause, preventing edge retriggering until release. A similar bug may exist for confirm-to-start transitions.\n\nThe confirm-to-start transition is not a bug. The pause bug is the main gameplay hole. I will check split-screen autoClear next.\n\nSplit-screen autoClear is plausible but unproven. HUD and viewports both use humans.length, so 4-player display is not broken. Four cameras are created per port and blend independently. Each camera starts at the origin and lerps separately, so they do not share state.\n\nThe pause bug is now fully traced. menuPrev is never updated during the race, so the next frame sees the held pause and keyboard back as fresh edges and immediately resumes. The pause menu is therefore unreachable.\n\nInverse-hull outlines use FrontSide instead of BackSide, so the scaled shell covers the cel-shaded chassis, torso, and head rather than drawing a silhouette. The CPU and player cannot throw a held item without releasing and re-pressing; this is acceptable design. A logic bug was also found: stepKart applies movement before projectProgress overwrites y, but projectProgress does not correct x or z, while wall collision properly handles those axes.\n\nDrift heading is applied correctly and normal steering is skipped. A real logic bug exists in the substep order: `noteLap` runs before `resolveCircuitWalls` executes its speed penalty. A player scraping a wall while crossing the finish line can have their speed crushed below 1 before the lap is registered, so the finish is missed.\n\nThe wall-crush lap bug is an edge case and will be skipped. Player 2 input indexing was verified as correct.\n\nThe nose is a sibling to the chassis shell, not a child. It extends 0.16 times the body depth past the shell's front edge, so it may remain visible outside the dark outline.\n\nWheels may also protrude past the shell. The torso and head are fully enclosed by their own shells, so the driver remains dark. The kart is therefore mostly invisible, confirming a real defect. Tests passed twice and launch logs agree.\n\nThe outline bug is a visual defect, not a code correctness failure. Cel shading is properly wired and used; the outline merely obscures it with a dark shell.\n\nThe outline bug is a concrete wrong result, not a style preference. The pause bug alone is sufficient to refute the cel-shading objective if the aggregator rejects visual issues. A third possible `inputs[index]` indexing bug was considered but not pursued. Battle-mode edge cases were skipped.\n\nThe pause bug is confirmed in the source: menuPrev is only updated inside the race branch, so the stale back edge immediately resumes the race on the next frame. No test covers this transition, which explains why it shipped undetected.\n\nThe findings will be structured as bugs, not gaps. The pause fix should be actionable: seed menuPrev with the current action when entering pause so the stale back edge cannot resume the race on the next frame. A regression test is also recommended to prevent the bug from recurring. For the outline, the material should be set to BackSide so the dark shell draws behind the cel-shaded mesh instead of covering it.\n\nThe outline material uses a unique color, so setting its side property is safe and will not affect other basic materials. The shell material may also need depthWrite disabled, but BackSide is the primary fix. Two findings are sufficient to refute the cel-shading objective.\n\nThe credits Testing Feedback claims the pause bug was already fixed: the Start edge is stored before it is read, so resume cannot trigger from it. The author believes the Resume row still handles resumption. This contradicts the earlier finding that menuPrev stays stale and immediately resumes the race on the next frame.\n\nThe credits claim the pause bug was fixed by storing the Start edge before reading it, which would prevent resume. That change is now understood to have only worked in a prior version where menuPrev was updated before the pauseEdge check. The current code still unpauses on the next frame because menuPrev is never latched during the race.\n\nThe credits claim the pause bug was fixed by moving menuPrev assignment after the pauseEdge check, which allows resume. The current code order does not match that description. The real issue is that menuPrev is never seeded when entering pause from the race, so the stale back edge still immediately resumes on the next frame.\n\nA third split-screen bug was considered but dropped because the output-pass scissor ambiguity is too unclear. A pixel-read test was also rejected since the plan forbids pixel grading and the launch never started a two-player race.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9d422824-6cd6-42ae-a629-da193355dcd5-53","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html","offset":2148,"limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9d422824-6cd6-42ae-a629-da193355dcd5-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/main.js","offset":808,"limit":70}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3138,"output_tokens":3805,"cache_read_input_tokens":124288,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"6eff9ac6-6660-41ff-9283-64a5f8651eff"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9d422824-6cd6-42ae-a629-da193355dcd5-53","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2148→  texture.colorSpace = THREE.NoColorSpace;\\n  texture.needsUpdate = true;\\n2150→  return texture;\\n}\\nfunction makeMaterials(gradient) {\\n  const cache = /* @__PURE__ */ new Map();\\n  function toon(color, side = THREE.FrontSide) {\\n    const key = `t${color}:${side}`;\\n    if (cache.has(key)) return cache.get(key);\\n    const material = new THREE.MeshToonNodeMaterial({ color, gradientMap: gradient, side });\\n    cache.set(key, material);\\n    return material;\\n2160→  }\\n  function basic(color) {\\n    const key = `b${color}`;\\n    if (cache.has(key)) return cache.get(key);\\n    const material = new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color });\\n    cache.set(key, material);\\n    return material;\\n  }\\n  return { toon, basic, outline: basic(1314840) };\\n}\\n2170→function addOutline(mesh) {\\n  const shell = new THREE.Mesh(mesh.geometry, mesh.userData.outlineMaterial);\\n  shell.scale.setScalar(1.045);\\n  shell.castShadow = false;\\n  shell.receiveShadow = false;\\n  mesh.add(shell);\\n}\\nfunction ribbon(course, half, lift) {\",\"content_concise\":\"2148→  texture.colorSpace = THREE.NoColorSpace;\\n  texture.needsUpdate = true;\\n2150→  return texture;\\n}\\nfunction makeMaterials(gradient) {\\n  const cache = /* @__PURE__ */ new Map();\\n  function toon(color, side = THREE.FrontSide) {\\n    const key = `t${color}:${side}`;\\n    if (cache.has(key)) return cache.get(key);\\n    const material = new THREE.MeshToonNodeMaterial({ color, gradientMap: gradient, side });\\n    cache.set(key, material);\\n    return material;\\n2160→  }\\n  function basic(color) {\\n    const key = `b${color}`;\\n    if (cache.has(key)) return cache.get(key);\\n    const material = new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color });\\n    cache.set(key, material);\\n    return material;\\n  }\\n  return { toon, basic, outline: basic(1314840) };\\n}\\n2170→function addOutline(mesh) {\\n  const shell = new THREE.Mesh(mesh.geometry, mesh.userData.outlineMaterial);\\n  shell.scale.setScalar(1.045);\\n  shell.castShadow = false;\\n  shell.receiveShadow = false;\\n  mesh.add(shell);\\n}\\nfunction ribbon(course, half, lift) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html\",\"offset\":2148,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"  texture.colorSpace = THREE.NoColorSpace;\\n  texture.needsUpdate = true;\\n  return texture;\\n}\\nfunction makeMaterials(gradient) {\\n  const cache = /* @__PURE__ */ new Map();\\n  function toon(color, side = THREE.FrontSide) {\\n    const key = `t${color}:${side}`;\\n    if (cache.has(key)) return cache.get(key);\\n    const material = new THREE.MeshToonNodeMaterial({ color, gradientMap: gradient, side });\\n    cache.set(key, material);\\n    return material;\\n  }\\n  function basic(color) {\\n    const key = `b${color}`;\\n    if (cache.has(key)) return cache.get(key);\\n    const material = new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color });\\n    cache.set(key, material);\\n    return material;\\n  }\\n  return { toon, basic, outline: basic(1314840) };\\n}\\nfunction addOutline(mesh) {\\n  const shell = new THREE.Mesh(mesh.geometry, mesh.userData.outlineMaterial);\\n  shell.scale.setScalar(1.045);\\n  shell.castShadow = false;\\n  shell.receiveShadow = false;\\n  mesh.add(shell);\\n}\\nfunction ribbon(course, half, lift) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":3581}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9d422824-6cd6-42ae-a629-da193355dcd5-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"808→    }\\n  }\\n810→  if (session.screen === \\\"race\\\" && race && !race.attract) {\\n    const humans = race.karts.filter((kart) => kart.isPlayer);\\n    const actions = humans.map((kart, index) => drivingActions({\\n      pad: pads[kart.playerIndex] || pads[index] || null,\\n      keys,\\n      mouse,\\n      settings: session.settings,\\n      playerIndex: kart.playerIndex || 0,\\n      useMouse: index === 0 && document.pointerLockElement === $(\\\"view\\\"),\\n    }));\\n820→    let paused = false;\\n    actions.forEach((action, index) => {\\n      const prev = drivePrev[index];\\n      if (action.camera && !prev.camera) {\\n        const at = CAM_CYCLE.indexOf(camModes[index] || \\\"chase\\\");\\n        camModes[index] = CAM_CYCLE[(at + 1) % CAM_CYCLE.length];\\n      }\\n      if (action.pause && !prev.pause) paused = true;\\n      drivePrev[index] = action;\\n    });\\n830→    if (paused) {\\n      session.screen = \\\"pause\\\";\\n      session.focus = 0;\\n      renderKey = \\\"\\\";\\n      renderAll();\\n    } else if (race.phase !== \\\"finished\\\") {\\n      stepRace(race, actions, dt);\\n      drainAudio();\\n      if (race.phase === \\\"finished\\\") enterResults();\\n    }\\n840→  } else if (session.screen === \\\"attract\\\" && race && !busy) {\\n    if (race.phase !== \\\"finished\\\") {\\n      stepRace(race, null, dt);\\n      drainAudio();\\n    } else {\\n      busy = true;\\n      launchAttract().finally(() => {\\n        busy = false;\\n      });\\n    }\\n850→  } else if (session.screen !== \\\"race\\\") {\\n    const menuAction = drivingActions({\\n      pad: pads[0] || null,\\n      keys,\\n      mouse: null,\\n      settings: session.settings,\\n      playerIndex: 0,\\n      useMouse: false,\\n    });\\n    const pauseEdge = session.screen === \\\"pause\\\" && menuAction.pause && !menuPrev.pause;\\n860→    if (!swallow && session.screen !== \\\"attract\\\") {\\n      const edgeX = menuAction.menuX && !menuPrev.menuX ? menuAction.menuX : 0;\\n      const edgeY = menuAction.menuY && !menuPrev.menuY ? menuAction.menuY : 0;\\n      const confirm = menuAction.confirm && !menuPrev.confirm;\\n      const back = menuAction.back