",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3f6ae741-638a-486f-b7c6-2b65ee9c31ee-56","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Verdict: Refuted\\n\\nThe slice is real: one root HTML, 50 titles with index 21 picked, WebGPU + Rapier 0.19.3, cel toon materials, and the node suite (14/14, twice) drives the shipped race modules. Launch logs agree on title, Grand Cup, a 1280×720 buffer, and a countdown HUD. Two shipped behaviors are still wrong.\\n\\n## Pause does not stay paused\\n\\n`src/main.js` enters pause from the race branch (`830-834`) and does not touch `menuPrev`. `menuPrev` is only written in the menu branch (`867`). The next frame the screen is `\\\"pause\\\"`, so that branch runs while Options / Escape is still down:\\n\\n- `pauseEdge` (`859`) is true because `menuPrev.pause` is still false.\\n- Keyboard Escape is also `back` (`input.js` player-0 keyset). `onMenuEdges` (`535-540`) treats back on the pause screen as resume.\\n- Then `868-871` sets the screen back to `\\\"race\\\"` anyway.\\n\\nA normal press lasts many frames. The pause menu (Resume / Quit) is painted for one frame and then dismissed. The credits note that the Start edge used to be stored before it was read; the current order checks the edge first, but never latches the button that opened pause. Seed `menuPrev` with the held pause/back when entering pause so resume is a later press.\\n\\n## Outlines hide the cel kart\\n\\n`makeMaterials` builds the outline as `MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color })` with no `side` (`scene.js:161-168`). `addOutline` (`171-176`) parents a 1.045-scaled shell of the same geometry. Default side is FrontSide, so the enlarged shell's front faces sit outside the chassis, torso, and head and depth-occlude the `MeshToonNodeMaterial`. The sky mesh correctly sets `THREE.BackSide` (`310`); the outline does not. Stack notes claim BackSide inverse-hull outlines. The bundled HTML matches the source (`basic(1314840)` then `scale.setScalar(1.045)`). Set the outline material to `BackSide` and rebuild the root HTML so the toon body stays visible.\\n\\n## What held\\n\\nFilename and dev folder, HTML comment plus About text (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback), no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/WebGLRenderer, file:// gate observed, attract idle constant, item/cup/battle/invert tests import the real modules, Rapier cone steps, both launch logs agree.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-classifier-17adb0589bdc-1-skeptic-0.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-classifier-17adb0589bdc-1-skeptic-0.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-classifier-17adb0589bdc-1-skeptic-0.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Verdict: Refuted\\n\\nThe slice is real: one root HTML, 50 titles with index 21 picked, WebGPU + Rapier 0.19.3, cel toon materials, and the node suite (14/14, twice) drives the shipped race modules. Launch logs agree on title, Grand Cup, a 1280×720 buffer, and a countdown HUD. Two shipped behaviors are still wrong.\\n\\n## Pause does not stay paused\\n\\n`src/main.js` enters pause from the race branch (`830-834`) and does not touch `menuPrev`. `menuPrev` is only written in the menu branch (`867`). The next frame the screen is `\\\"pause\\\"`, so that branch runs while Options / Escape is still down:\\n\\n- `pauseEdge` (`859`) is true because `menuPrev.pause` is still false.\\n- Keyboard Escape is also `back` (`input.js` player-0 keyset). `onMenuEdges` (`535-540`) treats back on the pause screen as resume.\\n- Then `868-871` sets the screen back to `\\\"race\\\"` anyway.\\n\\nA normal press lasts many frames. The pause menu (Resume / Quit) is painted for one frame and then dismissed. The credits note that the Start edge used to be stored before it was read; the current order checks the edge first, but never latches the button that opened pause. Seed `menuPrev` with the held pause/back when entering pause so resume is a later press.\\n\\n## Outlines hide the cel kart\\n\\n`makeMaterials` builds the outline as `MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color })` with no `side` (`scene.js:161-168`). `addOutline` (`171-176`) parents a 1.045-scaled shell of the same geometry. Default side is FrontSide, so the enlarged shell's front faces sit outside the chassis, torso, and head and depth-occlude the `MeshToonNodeMaterial`. The sky mesh correctly sets `THREE.BackSide` (`310`); the outline does not. Stack notes claim BackSide inverse-hull outlines. The bundled HTML matches the source (`basic(1314840)` then `scale.setScalar(1.045)`). Set the outline material to `BackSide` and rebuild the root HTML so the toon body stays visible.\\n\\n## What held\\n\\nFilename and dev folder, HTML comment plus About text (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback), no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/WebGLRenderer, file:// gate observed, attract idle constant, item/cup/battle/invert tests import the real modules, Rapier cone steps, both launch logs agree.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"2112d6dd-3278-47cd-99d9-971a3c256c8b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_121","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The schema marks `details_md` as optional. The aggregator falls back to the details file when this field is omitted.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-75ada011-a8f6-4e04-8362-881b4a854690-57","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-verdict-17adb0589bdc-1-0.json","old_string":"\"details_md\": \"See goal-classifier markdown.\"","new_string":"\"details_md\": \"# Verdict: Refuted\\n\\nThe slice is real: one root HTML, 50 titles with index 21 picked, WebGPU + Rapier 0.19.3, cel toon materials, and the node suite (14/14, twice) drives the shipped race modules. Launch logs agree on title, Grand Cup, a 1280×720 buffer, and a countdown HUD. Two shipped behaviors are still wrong.\\n\\n## Pause does not stay paused\\n\\n`src/main.js` enters pause from the race branch (830-834) and does not touch `menuPrev`. `menuPrev` is only written in the menu branch (867). The next frame the screen is `pause`, so that branch runs while Options / Escape is still down:\\n\\n- `pauseEdge` (859) is true because `menuPrev.pause` is still false.\\n- Keyboard Escape is also `back` (`input.js` player-0 keyset). `onMenuEdges` (535-540) treats back on the pause screen as resume.\\n- Then 868-871 sets the screen back to `race` anyway.\\n\\nA normal press lasts many frames. The pause menu (Resume / Quit) is painted for one frame and then dismissed. Seed `menuPrev` with the held pause/back when entering pause so resume is a later press.\\n\\n## Outlines hide the cel kart\\n\\n`makeMaterials` builds the outline as `MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color })` with no `side` (`scene.js:161-168`). `addOutline` (171-176) parents a 1.045-scaled shell of the same geometry. Default side is FrontSide, so the enlarged shell's front faces sit outside the chassis, torso, and head and depth-occlude the `MeshToonNodeMaterial`. The sky mesh correctly sets `THREE.BackSide` (310); the outline does not. Set the outline material to `BackSide` and rebuild the root HTML so the toon body stays visible.\\n\\n## What held\\n\\nFilename and dev folder, HTML comment plus About text (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback), no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/WebGLRenderer, file:// gate observed, attract idle constant, item/cup/battle/invert tests import the real modules, Rapier cone steps, both launch logs agree.\""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1731,"output_tokens":737,"cache_read_input_tokens":132224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"8bf46c9e-9144-43fd-890b-50556a349db1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-75ada011-a8f6-4e04-8362-881b4a854690-57","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\\\"details_md\\\": \\\"See goal-classifier markdown.\\\"\",\"new_string\":\"\\\"details_md\\\": \\\"# Verdict: Refuted\\\\n\\\\nThe slice is real: one root HTML, 50 titles with index 21 picked, WebGPU + Rapier 0.19.3, cel toon materials, and the node suite (14/14, twice) drives the shipped race modules. Launch logs agree on title, Grand Cup, a 1280×720 buffer, and a countdown HUD. Two shipped behaviors are still wrong.\\\\n\\\\n## Pause does not stay paused\\\\n\\\\n`src/main.js` enters pause from the race branch (830-834) and does not touch `menuPrev`. `menuPrev` is only written in the menu branch (867). The next frame the screen is `pause`, so that branch runs while Options / Escape is still down:\\\\n\\\\n- `pauseEdge` (859) is true because `menuPrev.pause` is still false.\\\\n- Keyboard Escape is also `back` (`input.js` player-0 keyset). `onMenuEdges` (535-540) treats back on the pause screen as resume.\\\\n- Then 868-871 sets the screen back to `race` anyway.\\\\n\\\\nA normal press lasts many frames. The pause menu (Resume / Quit) is painted for one frame and then dismissed. Seed `menuPrev` with the held pause/back when entering pause so resume is a later press.\\\\n\\\\n## Outlines hide the cel kart\\\\n\\\\n`makeMaterials` builds the outline as `MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color })` with no `side` (`scene.js:161-168`). `addOutline` (171-176) parents a 1.045-scaled shell of the same geometry. Default side is FrontSide, so the enlarged shell's front faces sit outside the chassis, torso, and head and depth-occlude the `MeshToonNodeMaterial`. The sky mesh correctly sets `THREE.BackSide` (310); the outline does not. Set the outline material to `BackSide` and rebuild the root HTML so the toon body stays visible.\\\\n\\\\n## What held\\\\n\\\\nFilename and dev folder, HTML comment plus About text (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback), no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/WebGLRenderer, file:// gate observed, attract idle constant, item/cup/battle/invert tests import the real modules, Rapier cone steps, both launch logs agree.\\\"\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-verdict-17adb0589bdc-1-0.json has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-verdict-17adb0589bdc-1-0.json has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-verdict-17adb0589bdc-1-0.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\\\"details_md\\\": \\\"See goal-classifier markdown.\\\"\",\"old_line\":18,\"new_string\":\"\\\"details_md\\\": \\\"# Verdict: Refuted\\\\n\\\\nThe slice is real: one root HTML, 50 titles with index 21 picked, WebGPU + Rapier 0.19.3, cel toon materials, and the node suite (14/14, twice) drives the shipped race modules. Launch logs agree on title, Grand Cup, a 1280×720 buffer, and a countdown HUD. Two shipped behaviors are still wrong.\\\\n\\\\n## Pause does not stay paused\\\\n\\\\n`src/main.js` enters pause from the race branch (830-834) and does not touch `menuPrev`. `menuPrev` is only written in the menu branch (867). The next frame the screen is `pause`, so that branch runs while Options / Escape is still down:\\\\n\\\\n- `pauseEdge` (859) is true because `menuPrev.pause` is still false.\\\\n- Keyboard Escape is also `back` (`input.js` player-0 keyset). `onMenuEdges` (535-540) treats back on the pause screen as resume.\\\\n- Then 868-871 sets the screen back to `race` anyway.\\\\n\\\\nA normal press lasts many frames. The pause menu (Resume / Quit) is painted for one frame and then dismissed. Seed `menuPrev` with the held pause/back when entering pause so resume is a later press.\\\\n\\\\n## Outlines hide the cel kart\\\\n\\\\n`makeMaterials` builds the outline as `MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ color })` with no `side` (`scene.js:161-168`). `addOutline` (171-176) parents a 1.045-scaled shell of the same geometry. Default side is FrontSide, so the enlarged shell's front faces sit outside the chassis, torso, and head and depth-occlude the `MeshToonNodeMaterial`. The sky mesh correctly sets `THREE.BackSide` (310); the outline does not. Set the outline material to `BackSide` and rebuild the root HTML so the toon body stays visible.\\\\n\\\\n## What held\\\\n\\\\nFilename and dev folder, HTML comment plus About text (Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback), no TODO/FIXME/placeholder/WebGLRenderer, file:// gate observed, attract idle constant, item/cup/battle/invert tests import the real modules, Rapier cone steps, both launch logs agree.\\\"\",\"new_line\":18,\"context_before\":\"  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Pause edge is computed from a menuPrev that the race branch never updates (main.js:830-871); outline material is MeshBasicNodeMaterial({color}) with default FrontSide (scene.js:161-172, HTML bundle lines 2161-2175). Unit logs 14/14 and launch DOM/canvas checks do not cover either path.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n\",\"context_after\":\"}\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"  \"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"0fa714b4-56c9-4fca-874e-274d308e5569"}
