uEdges(start, seedHeldMenu(start));\\n  assert.equal(start.pause, true);\\n  assert.equal(startHeld.pause, false);\\n  assert.equal(startHeld.back, false);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"outline shells use the back side so they do not cover the kart\\\", () => {\\n  const THREE = { BackSide: { id: \\\"back\\\" }, FrontSide: { id: \\\"front\\\" } };\\n  const options = outlineMaterialOptions(THREE);\\n  assert.equal(options.side, THREE.BackSide);\\n  assert.notEqual(options.side, THREE.FrontSide);\\n  assert.equal(options.color, 0x141018);\\n});\\n\\ntest(\\\"touch-only devices are told a controller or keyboard is required\\\", () => {\",\"new_line\":454,\"context_before\":\"  assert.equal(none.y, -0.2);\\n});\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"  assert.equal(TOUCH_MESSAGE, \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\");\\n  assert.equal(touchGateVisible({ coarsePointer: true, hover: false, maxTouchPoints: 5 }), true);\\n  assert.equal(touchGateVisible({ coarsePointer: false, hover: true, maxTouchPoints: 0 }), false);\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0fbc8f5f-fcd5-42db-8142-5d30c34bcc2b-149","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 1. The downward road would leave the course invisible. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The pause edge and the wall-hit repeat do not stop a race.\",\"new_string\":\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 2. The downward road would leave the course invisible. Outline shells were front-facing, so they covered the kart body; they now use the back side and only the silhouette shows. Pause also closed itself: the held pause key is also back, and the menu read that as a new press. Entering pause now latches that hold until the key comes up. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The wall-hit repeat does not stop a race.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 1. The downward road would leave the course invisible. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The pause edge and the wall-hit repeat do not stop a race.\",\"old_line\":14,\"new_string\":\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 2. The downward road would leave the course invisible. Outline shells were front-facing, so they covered the kart body; they now use the back side and only the silhouette shows. Pause also closed itself: the held pause key is also back, and the menu read that as a new press. Entering pause now latches that hold until the key comes up. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The wall-hit repeat does not stop a race.\",\"new_line\":14,\"context_before\":\"\\nTesting Feedback\\nHow many issues did testing catch? The first suite run failed 2 tests. One was a product timer: a single step longer than 3 seconds never finished a 5 second item-box return, because the race clamped each call to 3 seconds. The cap is now 8 seconds. The other failure was the test itself: the stick sample never crossed the menu threshold, so it compared 0 with -0. A frame check of the road strip found the triangles wound downward, which would hide the track from above. That winding is reversed and the suite now asserts an upward normal. The pause Start edge was stored before it was read, so it could not resume; the Resume row still could. Wall hits also fired on every step while a kart stayed against a wall; they now wait 0.4 seconds. The headless load lost the WebGPU device under the default GPU flags. Launching Chromium with Vulkan kept the device. The canvas then matched the window, and a cup race showed lap, place, and speed. The buffer is resized only when the window size changes.\\n\",\"context_after\":\"What was the most helpful test you ran? The item-class test. It starts a fresh race and checks that every shipped item changes speed, control, balloons, or a held item.\\nWhat was the least helpful test you ran? The touch-gate predicate. It only checks three booleans and never opens the page.\\n\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"00e0019f-3693-4ee4-b449-0ac796de17c4"}
