was the hardest thing to do? Fitting every item class and every mode into one HTML file, with the node tests importing those same modules and with no unfinished feature left in the source.\\nIf there was one test you could of run, what would that test be? A headed WebGPU frame that checks the kart nose points along its velocity and that the road is on screen. This run was not allowed to grade pixels, and the headless browser may not expose an adapter.\\n`;\\n\",\"total_lines\":31}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f3467a5e-2635-406e-b9f5-aa42888df5b9-157","content":"{\"type\":\"KillTask\",\"Result\":{\"task_id\":\"731ded61-8604-4178-b1dd-931655c16654\",\"outcome\":\"killed\",\"message\":\"Task was terminated successfully\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f3467a5e-2635-406e-b9f5-aa42888df5b9-158","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"Cel shading: MeshToonNodeMaterial (Three.js r180 WebGPU) with a 4-stop nearest DataTexture gradient in NoColorSpace. Outlines are inverse-hull meshes, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, BackSide, scale 1.045.\",\"new_string\":\"Cel shading: MeshToonNodeMaterial (Three.js r180 WebGPU) with a 4-stop nearest DataTexture gradient in NoColorSpace. Outlines are inverse-hull meshes on the chassis, torso, and head: MeshBasicNodeMaterial, side BackSide, scale 1.045. FrontSide would cover the cel body.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/stack-notes.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/stack-notes.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/stack-notes.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"Cel shading: MeshToonNodeMaterial (Three.js r180 WebGPU) with a 4-stop nearest DataTexture gradient in NoColorSpace. Outlines are inverse-hull meshes, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, BackSide, scale 1.045.\",\"old_line\":3,\"new_string\":\"Cel shading: MeshToonNodeMaterial (Three.js r180 WebGPU) with a 4-stop nearest DataTexture gradient in NoColorSpace. Outlines are inverse-hull meshes on the chassis, torso, and head: MeshBasicNodeMaterial, side BackSide, scale 1.045. FrontSide would cover the cel body.\",\"new_line\":3,\"context_before\":\"# Stack notes\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\nAnimation: the render loop calls animateScene. Wheels spin from speed, drivers bob and lean with steer, item crates tumble, boost flames and drift sparks flicker, and held items and balloons float.\\n\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"d75d9a74-84cc-4f7a-87cd-98efadf510af"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_131","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The testing feedback in the credits is inconsistent. The first paragraph still describes the old pause edge bug, while the critical paragraph says pause closed itself.\n\nBoth descriptions are accurate but describe different bugs. The HTML rebuild included the updated credits. I will now provide the final reply with the three required sections.\n\nThe first testing paragraph still describes the old pause edge bug. The hold latch issue was also fixed. The critical count says \"2\" but lists three issues: road, outline, and pause.\n\nI will correct the critical count from \"2\" to \"3\" in the credits and rebuild the HTML so the comment matches. The launch logs may be slightly stale on the about text, but the verifier might reload the file.\n\nI will rebuild the HTML after correcting the critical count to \"3\" and relaunch the game to verify the shipped file. The about text changes will not affect prior launch logs, but fresh evidence will be generated.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The credits counted two game-breaking bugs and then described three. I'll correct that count and rebuild so the page matches."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3f77eb38-7e24-4169-9da9-452e7cd552c0-159","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js","old_string":"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 2. The downward road would leave the course invisible. Outline shells were front-facing, so they covered the kart body; they now use the back side and only the silhouette shows. Pause also closed itself: the held pause key is also back, and the menu read that as a new press. Entering pause now latches that hold until the key comes up. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The wall-hit repeat does not stop a race.","new_string":"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 3. The downward road would leave the course invisible. Outline shells were front-facing, so they covered the kart body; they now use the back side and only the silhouette shows. Pause also closed itself on the same press: the held pause key is also back, and the menu read that as a new press. Entering pause now latches that hold until the key comes up. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The wall-hit repeat does not stop a race."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3f77eb38-7e24-4169-9da9-452e7cd552c0-160","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 -m http.server 8767 --bind 127.0.0.1","description":"Serve the rebuilt page for launch checks","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1730,"output_tokens":1020,"cache_read_input_tokens":181760,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"3b50d138-2703-4c72-b894-0980aaa565ae"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3f77eb38-7e24-4169-9da9-452e7cd552c0-159","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 2. The downward road would leave the course invisible. Outline shells were front-facing, so they covered the kart body; they now use the back side and only the silhouette shows. Pause also closed itself: the held pause key is also back, and the menu read that as a new press. Entering pause now latches that hold until the key comes up. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The wall-hit repeat does not stop a race.\",\"new_string\":\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 3. The downward road would leave the course invisible. Outline shells were front-facing, so they covered the kart body; they now use the back side and only the silhouette shows. Pause also closed itself on the same press: the held pause key is also back, and the menu read that as a new press. Entering pause now latches that hold until the key comes up. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The wall-hit repeat does not stop a race.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/credits.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 2. The downward road would leave the course invisible. Outline shells were front-facing, so they covered the kart body; they now use the back side and only the silhouette shows. Pause also closed itself: the held pause key is also back, and the menu read that as a new press. Entering pause now latches that hold until the key comes up. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The wall-hit repeat does not stop a race.\",\"old_line\":14,\"new_string\":\"How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking? 3. The downward road would leave the course invisible. Outline shells were front-facing, so they covered the kart body; they now use the back side and only the silhouette shows. Pause also closed itself on the same press: the held pause key is also back, and the menu read that as a new press. Entering pause now latches that hold until the key comes up. The timer cap does not bite at frame rate. The wall-hit repeat does not stop a race.\",\"new_line\":14,\"context_before\":\"\\nTesting Feedback\\nHow many issues did testing catch? The first suite run failed 2 tests. One was a product timer: a single step longer than 3 seconds never finished a 5 second item-box return, because the race clamped each call to 3 seconds. The cap is now 8 seconds. The other failure was the test itself: the stick sample never crossed the menu threshold, so it compared 0 with -0. A frame check of the road strip found the triangles wound downward, which would hide the track from above. That winding is reversed and the suite now asserts an upward normal. The pause Start edge was stored before it was read, so it could not resume; the Resume row still could. Wall hits also fired on every step while a kart stayed against a wall; they now wait 0.4 seconds. The headless load lost the WebGPU device under the default GPU flags. Launching Chromium with Vulkan kept the device. The canvas then matched the window, and a cup race showed lap, place, and speed. The buffer is resized only when the window size changes.\\n\",\"context_after\":\"What was the most helpful test you ran? The item-class test. It starts a fresh race and checks that every shipped item changes speed, control, balloons, or a held item.\\nWhat was the least helpful test you ran? The touch-gate predicate. It only checks three booleans and never opens the page.\\n\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3f77eb38-7e24-4169-9da9-452e7cd552c0-160","content":"{\"type\":\"BackgroundTaskStarted\",\"task_id\":\"7bccd2b8-fc79-4c1b-afb2-37fda827251b\",\"task_type\":\"bash\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on%2Fwork/01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862/terminal/call-3f77eb38-7e24-4169-9da9-452e7cd552c0-160.log\",\"status\":\"running\",\"command\":\"python3 -m http.server 8767 --bind 127.0.0.1\",\"summary\":\"Background task 7bccd2b8-fc79-4c1b-afb2-37fda827251b started\",\"retrieval_hint\":\"Use get_command_or_subagent_output with task_ids=[\\\"7bccd2b8-fc79-4c1b-afb2-37fda827251b\\\"] when you need the output.\",\"pid\":143702}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"a90f48a3-be6e-410c-bd19-4882706e15f5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_132","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Rebuilding and launching. Existing 16-pass unit tests remain valid since they do not cover credits text.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e61a429c-c57a-49fb-bfe9-e4935968d292-161","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637 && node build.mjs && export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64\nfor i in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8; do curl -sf -o /dev/null http://127.0.0.1:8767/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html && break; sleep 0.25; done\npython3 /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/launch.py \"http://127.0.0.1:8767/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html\" /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/launch-1.log\npython3 /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/launch.py \"http://127.0.0.1:8767/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html\" /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/launch-2.log\npython3 - << 'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot = Path(\"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer\")\nhtml = Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html\").read_text()\nprint(\"critical 3\", \"game breaking? 3.\" in html)\nprint(\"back side\", \"back side\" in html)\nfor name in [\"launch-1.log\", \"launch-2.log\"]:\n    data = json.loads((root / name).read_text())\n    err = [line for line in data[\"log\"] if \"error\" in line.lower() or line.startswith(\"pageerror\")]\n    print(name, data[\"title\"][\"boot\"], data[\"title\"][\"title\"], data[\"title\"][\"start\"], data[\"race\"][\"canvasWidth\"], data[\"race\"][\"clientWidth\"], data[\"race\"][\"bodyText\"].splitlines()[1], err)\nPY","description":"Rebuild credits and reload the page twice","block_until_ms":120000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1434,"output_tokens":734,"cache_read_input_tokens":183424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"1929d414-30c2-4e52-aa76-d736a2e1ae0d"}
