 you drive it again.\\\\n\\\\nVersus\\\\nTime Trial\\\\nBalloon Battle\\\\nHow to Drive\\\\nSettings\\\\nAbout\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"race\\\": {\\n    \\\"boot\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Kartesian Derby\\\",\\n    \\\"start\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"startId\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"gateHidden\\\": true,\\n    \\\"gateText\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"touchText\\\": \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\\n  Settings\\\",\\n    \\\"href\\\": \\\"http://127.0.0.1:8767/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html\\\",\\n    \\\"protocol\\\": \\\"http:\\\",\\n    \\\"secure\\\": true,\\n    \\\"hasGpu\\\": true,\\n    \\\"canvasWidth\\\": 1280,\\n    \\\"canvasHeight\\\": 720,\\n    \\\"clientWidth\\\": 1280,\\n    \\\"clientHeight\\\": 720,\\n    \\\"bodyText\\\": \\\"1st\\\\nLap 1 / 3\\\\n0 km/h\\\\nEmpty\\\\n1 Pip\\\\n2 Pip 1\\\\n3 Quill\\\\n4 Bramble\\\\n5 Holt\\\\n6 Pip 5\\\\n7 Quill 6\\\\n8 Bramble 7\\\\n\\\\n3\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"log\\\": [\\n    \\\"console.warning: using deprecated parameters for the initialization function; pass a single object instead\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\",\"total_lines\":41}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"bf87d92d-5113-4446-a5ed-40d583bf79c6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_138","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to examine seedHeldMenu more carefully.\n\nseedHeldMenu forces pause to true while spreading held. For Escape, held.back is already true, so menuEdges correctly returns false for both pause and back.\n\nGamepad Options also behaves correctly. The forced pause: true in seedHeldMenu is safe because that function only runs when entering pause, so the button that opened it is already held.\n\nI checked a cross-player edge case. If player 2 presses Enter to open pause while player 0 holds Enter, seedHeldMenu forces pause to true. The next frame still shows no pause edge because menuAction.pause remains false.\n\nReleasing Enter while paused leaves all edges false. A second press triggers confirm and resume via activate, not pauseEdge. Keyboard Escape also behaves correctly: seedHeldMenu forces both pause and back true, so no edges fire while held.\n\nGamepad pause resumes correctly on the second press. Steering input latches during pause, so menuY stays zero on the first menu frame. seedHeldMenu does not force back: true, but Escape already sets it.\n\nThe tests verify the pure functions that the frame loop invokes, which is a valid approach. The outline test checks that outlineMaterialOptions returns BackSide for use with MeshBasicNodeMaterial.\n\nThe HTML bundle now passes `THREE2.BackSide` into `outlineMaterialOptions`. The shell scale remains 1.045. This closes the prior gap.\n\nThe outline test may be slightly theatrical. It passes a fake THREE object and only checks the options object. It does not verify that `MeshBasicNodeMaterial` actually receives the side parameter. The scene code clearly wires the output into the material constructor.\n\nThe outline material is wired through mesh.userData.outlineMaterial. The basic() cache key includes the side parameter, and BackSide resolves to 1 while FrontSide resolves to 0.\n\nMeshBasicNodeMaterial receives both the side option and a direct material.side assignment, so the outline fix is fully covered. The menuEdges logic matches the previous implementation exactly, confirming no regression.\n\nThe pause screen logic redundantly sets the race screen from both onMenuEdges and pauseEdge. This is harmless.\n\nA potential bug was spotted: if a player taps pause so quickly that the key is already released by the next frame, seedHeldMenu still forces pause to true because it only runs when entering pause.\n\nThe quick-tap concern is resolved. If the pause key is already released by the next frame, menuAction shows no pause or back edges, so the pause screen stays active until a second press. seedHeldMenu only runs when entering pause, and keys remain down during that same frame.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule prevents hunting for new bugs. Only demonstrable defects in shipped behavior or unmet gating criteria are valid grounds to raise an objection.\n\nA potential bug was spotted in seedHeldMenu. Space serves as both hop and confirm during the race. If a player holds Space while pressing Escape to pause, seedHeldMenu copies held.confirm into the menu state. This could trigger an unintended confirm edge when the pause screen first appears.\n\nThe Space-and-pause edge case is harmless. While Escape and Space are both held, no confirm edge fires because menuPrev already matches. Releasing Escape first keeps the screen paused; releasing Space later allows a normal resume press.\n\nFlame materials use MeshBasicNodeMaterial directly and bypass basic(), so they remain unaffected by the FrontSide default.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-563b4896-6ba4-4939-8a0a-5f5c66fab638-73","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637.html","offset":2118,"limit":85}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-563b4896-