{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_155","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1f36a262-8a6b-403e-994b-19a7e84d91f0-30","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-verdict-17adb0589bdc-2-2.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"Pause seeds menuPrev via seedHeldMenu (main.js:830-840, input.js:126-128) so a held Escape/Start is not a rising back/pause edge; outline shells use outlineMaterialOptions BackSide (look.js:3-4, scene.js:53-62, 226-253). Bundled HTML matches (seedHeldMenu ~957, BackSide ~2129, menuPrev seed ~3487). unit-tests-1/2.log: 16 pass twice; launch-1/2.log agree on Kartesian Derby, Grand Cup, 1280x720, lap/place/speed.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"Not refuted. Both prior gaps are fixed in the modules the page bundles, and the root HTML was rebuilt with the same code.\\n\\nPause: entering pause copies the still-held player-0 action into `menuPrev` through `seedHeldMenu`, which spreads `pause` and `back` and forces `pause: true` (`src/main.js` 830-840, `src/input.js` 124-128). The next frame's `menuEdges` therefore sees no rising pause or back while Escape (pause and back) or Start stays down, so `onMenuEdges` does not resume and the pause-edge resume at `main.js` 875-878 does not fire. A later press after release still resumes. The node test drives `actionsFromKeys` / `actionsFromPad`, `seedHeldMenu`, and `menuEdges` on that path and passed in both suite logs.\\n\\nOutlines: `outlineMaterialOptions` returns `THREE.BackSide`; `makeMaterials` builds the shared outline `MeshBasicNodeMaterial` with that side; chassis, torso, and head parent a 1.045 shell of that material (`src/look.js` 3-4, `src/scene.js` 45-62 and 221-253). The bundle contains the same `BackSide` call and `seedHeldMenu` wiring. The outline test calls the shipped helper, not a copy.\\n\\nGating evidence from this round still holds: both unit logs are 16 pass / 0 fail, and both localhost launches show title Kartesian Derby, Grand Cup, canvas 1280x720 matching layout, and a cup HUD with lap, place, and speed, with only the known Rapier deprecation warning.\"\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1f36a262-8a6b-403e-994b-19a7e84d91f0-31","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-classifier-17adb0589bdc-2-skeptic-2.md","content":"# Skeptic verdict: Not refuted\n\nBoth prior gaps are fixed in the modules the page bundles, and the root HTML was rebuilt with the same code.\n\n## Pause stays open\n\nEntering pause copies the still-held player-0 action into `menuPrev` through `seedHeldMenu`, which spreads `pause` and `back` and forces `pause: true` (`src/main.js` 830-840, `src/input.js` 124-128). The next frame's `menuEdges` therefore sees no rising pause or back while Escape (pause and back) or Start stays down, so `onMenuEdges` does not resume and the pause-edge resume at `main.js` 875-878 does not fire. A later press after release still resumes. The node test drives `actionsFromKeys` / `actionsFromPad`, `seedHeldMenu`, and `menuEdges` on that path and passed in both suite logs.\n\n## Outlines are BackSide\n\n`outlineMaterialOptions` returns `THREE.BackSide`. `makeMaterials` builds the shared outline `MeshBasicNodeMaterial` with that side. Chassis, torso, and head parent a 1.045 shell of that material (`src/look.js` 3-4, `src/scene.js` 45-62 and 221-253). The bundle contains the same `BackSide` call and `seedHeldMenu` wiring. The outline test calls the shipped helper, not a copy.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `unit-tests-1.log` and `unit-tests-2.log`: 16 pass, 0 fail, including the held-pause and BackSide tests.\n- `launch-1.log` and `launch-2.log` agree: title Kartesian Derby, Grand Cup present, canvas 1280×720 matching layout, cup HUD with lap, place, and speed. Only the known Rapier deprecation warning.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2263,"output_tokens":1451,"cache_read_input_tokens":47872,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"ae5e4e64-1da2-432c-ad6e-c472250a061c"}
