10,100,111,119,46,97,100,100,69,118,101,110,116,76,105,115,116,101,110,101,114,40,34,107,101,121,117,112,34,44,32,40,101,118,101,110,116,41,32,61,62,32,123,10,54,57,49,58,32,32,32,32,107,101,121,115,91,101,118,101,110,116,46,99,111,100,101,93,32,61,32,102,97,108,115,101,59,10,54,57,52,58,32,32,32,32,102,111,114,32,40,99,111,110,115,116,32,99,111,100,101,32,111,102,32,79,98,106,101,99,116,46,107,101,121,115,40,107,101,121,115,41,41,32,107,101,121,115,91,99,111,100,101,93,32,61,32,102,97,108,115,101,59,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":7,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh__example__v2__cel__free__efficient__on/work/Kartesian-Derby-Mario-Kart-64-for-N64-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261027-1637/src/main.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":43,\"content\":\"const keys = Object.create(null);\"},{\"line_number\":73,\"content\":\"  if (Object.keys(keys).some((code) => keys[code])) return true;\"},{\"line_number\":685,\"content\":\"  window.addEventListener(\\\"keydown\\\", (event) => {\"},{\"line_number\":686,\"content\":\"    keys[event.code] = true;\"},{\"line_number\":690,\"content\":\"  window.addEventListener(\\\"keyup\\\", (event) => {\"},{\"line_number\":691,\"content\":\"    keys[event.code] = false;\"},{\"line_number\":694,\"content\":\"    for (const code of Object.keys(keys)) keys[code] = false;\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"76140044-62c5-423d-82c0-743db04b151d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_160","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Mapping the Escape key to true in a keys object.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Prior pause and outline gaps are fixed in the shipped modules and the rebuilt HTML, and the captured tests and launches still match the plan."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a24ac532-7ad8-4494-846f-826321decafe-33","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-verdict-17adb0589bdc-2-1.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"main.js:830-840 seeds menuPrev via seedHeldMenu (input.js:126-128) so a held Escape is not a back/pause edge; scene.js:53-62 and look.js:3-4 build BackSide inverse-hull shells; both are in the rebuilt root HTML; unit-tests-1/2.log pass 16/16 including those cases; launch-1/2.log agree on Kartesian Derby, Grand Cup, and a 1280×720 cup HUD.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"Both prior gaps are fixed in the modules the page bundles and in the rebuilt root HTML. Entering pause copies the held pause and back state into `menuPrev` before the next frame's menu edges, so Resume and Quit stay reachable until the opening press is released. Outline shells use `THREE.BackSide` at 1.045 scale on the chassis, torso, and head. The unit suite passed twice (16 tests, including the new pause-latch and outline cases) and both localhost loads agreed: title Kartesian Derby, Grand Cup present, canvas 1280×720, cup HUD showing lap, place, and speed.\"\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a24ac532-7ad8-4494-846f-826321decafe-34","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-classifier-17adb0589bdc-2-skeptic-1.md","content":"# Verification\n\nNot refuted. Both prior gaps are fixed in the shipped modules and in the rebuilt root HTML. Gating criteria from the plan still hold.\n\n## Prior gap: pause\n\n`frame` sets `session.screen = \"pause\"` and immediately latches the held action:\n\n- `Kartesian-Derby-…/src/main.js:830-840` assigns `menuPrev = seedHeldMenu(drivingActions({…}))` on the same frame that opens pause, inside the race branch, so the menu edge path does not run until the next frame.\n- `src/input.js:126-128` `seedHeldMenu` copies the held action (including `back`, which Escape also sets) and forces `pause: true`.\n- `menuEdges` (`src/input.js:112-121`) only reports a rising edge. The next frame, while Escape or Start is still down, `edges.back` and `edges.pause` are false, so `onMenuEdges` does not resume (`main.js:534-540`) and `pauseEdge` does not (`main.js:867-878`).\n- After release, a second Escape is both pause and back and resumes. Confirm on the pause rows (`main.js:235-238`, `458-460`) still reaches Resume and Quit to title.\n- The same latch is in the bundled HTML at lines 957-958 and 3484-3494.\n\n`test/game.test.mjs:454-475` drives the real `actionsFromKeys`, `actionsFromPad`, `seedHeldMenu`, and `menuEdges`. Held Escape yields no pause or back edge; a press after release does. Gamepad button 9 is latched the same way.\n\n## Prior gap: outlines\n\n- `src/look.js:3-4` returns `{ side: THREE.BackSide }`.\n- `src/scene.js:53-54` builds the shared outline material with that side and sets `material.side`.\n- `addOutline` (`scene.js:57-62`) scales the shell to 1.045 and parents it. Chassis, torso, and head assign `userData.outlineMaterial = mats.outline` before the call (`scene.js:225-253`).\n- The rebuilt HTML contains `outlineMaterialOptions` returning `THREE2.BackSide` (lines 2128-2129 and 2190-2198).\n\n`test/game.test.mjs:478-483` asserts the shipped options use `BackSide`, not `FrontSide`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/unit-tests-1.log` and `unit-tests-2.log` (17:48): 16 pass, 0 fail, including the pause-latch and outline tests. Same assertions both runs.\n- `launch-1.log` and `launch-2.log` (17:48): both `http://127.0.0.1:8767/…html`, boot ready, title \"Kartesian Derby\", start \"Grand Cup\", canvas 1280×720 matching client size, cup body text `1st / Lap 1 / 3 / 0 km/h`. Only console line is the known Rapier init deprecation warning.\n- Plan diff only checks off completed tasks. It does not weaken acceptance criteria.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, or `WebGLRenderer` in the root HTML. Top comment and About text include Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback. The final reply includes the three required sections.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":619,"output_tokens":1311,"cache_read_input_tokens":56192,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a17fba-2fc3-7d53-9fa6-699993e68862","uuid":"63e00b7e-0eb3-49cf-b05a-36b5d3d00859"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a24ac532-7ad8-4494-846f-826321decafe-33","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": false,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"main.js:830-840 seeds menuPrev via seedHeldMenu (input.js:126-128) so a held Escape is not a back/pause edge; scene.js:53-62 and look.js:3-4 build BackSide inverse-hull shells; both are in the rebuilt root HTML; unit-tests-1/2.log pass 16/16 including those cases; launch-1/2.log agree on Kartesian Derby, Grand Cup, and a 1280×720 cup HUD.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"Both prior gaps are fixed in the modules the page bundles and in the rebuilt root HTML. Entering pause copies the held pause and back state into `menuPrev` before the next frame's menu edges, so Resume and Quit stay reachable until the opening press is released. Outline shells use `THREE.BackSide` at 1.045 scale on the chassis, torso, and head. The unit suite passed twice (16 tests, including the new pause-latch and outline cases) and both localhost loads agreed: title Kartesian Derby, Grand Cup present, canvas 1280×720, cup HUD showing lap, place, and speed.\\\"\\n}\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-verdict-17adb0589bdc-2-1.json has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-verdict-17adb0589bdc-2-1.json has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-verdict-17adb0589bdc-2-1.json\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"{\\n  \\\"refuted\\\": false,\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"main.js:830-840 seeds menuPrev via seedHeldMenu (input.js:126-128) so a held Escape is not a back/pause edge; scene.js:53-62 and look.js:3-4 build BackSide inverse-hull shells; both are in the rebuilt root HTML; unit-tests-1/2.log pass 16/16 including those cases; launch-1/2.log agree on Kartesian Derby, Grand Cup, and a 1280×720 cup HUD.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"blocking\\\": \\\"none\\\",\\n  \\\"details_md\\\": \\\"Both prior gaps are fixed in the modules the page bundles and in the rebuilt root HTML. Entering pause copies the held pause and back state into `menuPrev` before the next frame's menu edges, so Resume and Quit stay reachable until the opening press is released. Outline shells use `THREE.BackSide` at 1.045 scale on the chassis, torso, and head. The unit suite passed twice (16 tests, including the new pause-latch and outline cases) and both localhost loads agreed: title Kartesian Derby, Grand Cup present, canvas 1280×720, cup HUD showing lap, place, and speed.\\\"\\n}\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a24ac532-7ad8-4494-846f-826321decafe-34","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Verification\\n\\nNot refuted. Both prior gaps are fixed in the shipped modules and in the rebuilt root HTML. Gating criteria from the plan still hold.\\n\\n## Prior gap: pause\\n\\n`frame` sets `session.screen = \\\"pause\\\"` and immediately latches the held action:\\n\\n- `Kartesian-Derby-…/src/main.js:830-840` assigns `menuPrev = seedHeldMenu(drivingActions({…}))` on the same frame that opens pause, inside the race branch, so the menu edge path does not run until the next frame.\\n- `src/input.js:126-128` `seedHeldMenu` copies the held action (including `back`, which Escape also sets) and forces `pause: true`.\\n- `menuEdges` (`src/input.js:112-121`) only reports a rising edge. The next frame, while Escape or Start is still down, `edges.back` and `edges.pause` are false, so `onMenuEdges` does not resume (`main.js:534-540`) and `pauseEdge` does not (`main.js:867-878`).\\n- After release, a second Escape is both pause and back and resumes. Confirm on the pause rows (`main.js:235-238`, `458-460`) still reaches Resume and Quit to title.\\n- The same latch is in the bundled HTML at lines 957-958 and 3484-3494.\\n\\n`test/game.test.mjs:454-475` drives the real `actionsFromKeys`, `actionsFromPad`, `seedHeldMenu`, and `menuEdges`. Held Escape yields no pause or back edge; a press after release does. Gamepad button 9 is latched the same way.\\n\\n## Prior gap: outlines\\n\\n- `src/look.js:3-4` returns `{ side: THREE.BackSide }`.\\n- `src/scene.js:53-54` builds the shared outline material with that side and sets `material.side`.\\n- `addOutline` (`scene.js:57-62`) scales the shell to 1.045 and parents it. Chassis, torso, and head assign `userData.outlineMaterial = mats.outline` before the call (`scene.js:225-253`).\\n- The rebuilt HTML contains `outlineMaterialOptions` returning `THREE2.BackSide` (lines 2128-2129 and 2190-2198).\\n\\n`test/game.test.mjs:478-483` asserts the shipped options use `BackSide`, not `FrontSide`.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- `/tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/implementer/unit-tests-1.log` and `unit-tests-2.log` (17:48): 16 pass, 0 fail, including the pause-latch and outline tests. Same assertions both runs.\\n- `launch-1.log` and `launch-2.log` (17:48): both `http://127.0.0.1:8767/…html`, boot ready, title \\\"Kartesian Derby\\\", start \\\"Grand Cup\\\", canvas 1280×720 matching client size, cup body text `1st / Lap 1 / 3 / 0 km/h`. Only console line is the known Rapier init deprecation warning.\\n- Plan diff only checks off completed tasks. It does not weaken acceptance criteria.\\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, or `WebGLRenderer` in the root HTML. Top comment and About text include Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback. The final reply includes the three required sections.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /tmp/grok-goal-17adb0589bdc/goal-classifie